-- Quest text collected by LorePath's players (see issue #14), for quests the
-- bundled vanilla text doesn't cover, such as WoW Forever's own. Seeded from a
-- player's saved quest history; edit with care.
-- Fields: t title, o objectives, d description, p progress, c completion.
-- $N/$C/$R/$G/$B are filled in game.
local _, ns = ...
ns.CommunityText = {
[63]={t="Call of Water",o="Defeat the Corrupt Manifestation of Water and place the Corrupted Manifestation's Bracers along with the Remaining Drops of Purest Water on the Brazier of Everfount in Silverpine Forest.",d="Along the coast of Silverpine, west of the Sepulcher, you will find a shrine that has become tainted by the plague. The spirits there no longer speak to our people and it will be up to you to defeat the manifestation and cleanse the pool.\n\nTake the elemental's bracers, along with the remaining drops of Brine's potion, and place them on the brazier. The ritual should be enough to summon a pure spirit for you to communicate with.\n\nBring me proof the task is done, and I will reward you with your totem.",p="The brazier still reflects the ambient light from the area, and the flame shifts slightly as you move closer.\n\nThe corruption along the hills seems to have kept its distance, and besides the missing components, the brazier looks prepared for the ritual to summon a cleansed manifestation of water.",c="You place the bracers atop the brazier and then pour the remaining drops of Brine's potion into the flame. The drops crackle as they hit the flame and you begin to incant the simple words Islen taught you...."},
[96]={t="Call of Water",o="Bring the Shard of Water to Islen Waterseer in the Barrens.",d="Take shard. Take shard and give life.\n\nGive life and understand. Understand water is life... corruption stops life.\n\nYou protect and give life with water's power.",p="You've returned. Splendid!\n\nHow went your journey to Silverpine? Did it take you long?\n\nIt is hard for me to tell if you were successful there because so much of the land has become corrupt. Its stench overwhelms any good that you might have done. But small successes are sometimes as important as large ones. Purifying the water there was instrumental for you, and for all shamans.",c="This is the proof I asked for. You've done well, $N.\n\nI am pleased to be the first to congratulate you and give you this... your water totem.\n\nUse it well, and good luck.\n\nYour next test will not be for some time, so learn your lessons well. Pure water will not only give life back to those who are injured, but can have many other effects. I suggest you seek out a shaman trainer when you have the time. They might have other spells for you to learn."},
[100]={t="Call of Water",o="Speak to the Minor Manifestation of Water in Silverpine Forest.",d="Light explodes as you finish the incantation. The sounds of the water drops hitting the flame have died down and your senses are overcome as the corrupt spirits around you are destroyed.",c="Thanks to you. Thanks to the shamans.\n\nCorruption ebbs but life continues to wane. Up to shamans to protect life."},
[220]={t="Call of Water",o="Bring the Vial of Purest Water to Islen Waterseer in the Barrens.",d="Islen will have one more task for you before rewarding you with your next totem. The vial of water I've given you is necessary for whatever that task is.\n\nGo now and find her. We shall meet again some day.",p="Hello again, $N. You're looking well.\n\nWhat brings you back to me so soon?",c="Ah, a vial of water created and blessed by Brine, and gathered by you, no less.\n\nThe liquid in this vial will be key in creating a sapta for you, but also used in one other task.\n\nThe sapta I create for you should be used to see the water spirits at the shrine in Silverpine Forest, south of the Undercity. The remaining drops, well, the remaining drops I will tell you about if you feel you are ready.\n\nAre you prepared for one more journey, $N?"},
[264]={t="Until Death Do Us Part",o="Place Clarice's Pendant on Yuriv's Tomb in Silverpine.",d="Filthy scum! Leaves me for his damn crusade. Because \"the Light is the most important thing we have against the threats the undead pose.\"\n\nWell, what about his children?! What about ME?! Night after night I sat patiently waiting for him... always second to his blasted duty!\n\nWell, witness what \"justice\" brings you, $N! He's dead and I'm bearing the very thing he was trying to stop!\n\nTake this piece of junk and put it on his tomb at the Sepulcher. I want nothing to do with it anymore... or him!"},
[356]={t="Rear Guard Patrol",o="Kill 8 Bleeding Horrors and 8 Wandering Spirits, then report back to Linnea at her camp.",d="The defenders on The Bulwark protecting Tirisfal from the Plaguelands are on constant alert. But sometimes Scourge will slip past them.\n\nOur success at the Bulwark depends on a one-front battle - we cannot allow an attack from the rear, nor can we allow our defenders' supply line to be cut.\n\nAssist the Bulwark. Patrol east and slay any Scourge you find. Spend particular effort at the Balnir Farmstead to the east. It has become a haven for interloping Scourge.",c="Very good. Your efforts do much to keep the Scourge at bay. A commendation will be sent to my superior, Executor Zygand."},
[447]={t="A Recipe For Death",o="Collect 6 Grizzled Bear Hearts and 6 samples of Skittering Blood and deliver them to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity.",d="Arthas's numbers are overwhelming. But with a New Plague we could eradicate both the Scourge Army and the Human infestation once and for all.\n\nMy studies have proven that spider blood combined with a toxin derived from a grizzled bear heart results in a deadly elixir. Collect samples from the spiders in the Skittering Dark to the northwest and from the bears wandering throughout Silverpine Forest. Deliver the reagents to Master Apothecary Faranell of the Royal Apothecary Society in the Undercity.",p="Hail, $C.  What business do you have with the Royal Apothecary Society?",c="How good of Apothecary Renferrel to send you to me, $N.  These samples will indeed prove useful to the cause.  I will begin studying their toxic and contaminable properties at once."},
[450]={t="A Recipe For Death",o="Retrieve Apothecary Berard's journal from Pyrewood Village and take it to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher.",d="You can be of further service to the Royal Apothecary Society, $N.\n\nWhen Arugal cast his wretched magic on the forest, he cursed one of our most promising members, Apothecary Berard.  Now a mindless servant of Arugal, Berard is useless to us.  But his findings might prove to be of worth.  He was studying an ancient plague that killed off all the aquatic life in Lake Lordamere ages ago.\n\nRetrieve Berard's Journal from his study in the Pyrewood Village Inn and take it to Apothecary Renferrel.",p="I see you are back, $N.",c="Apothecary Berard's journal!  Why you are quite brave, $N.  Now let's see what Berard was up to before he went mad. . ."},
[451]={t="A Recipe For Death",o="Bring 6 samples of Lake Creeper Moss, 6 samples of Lake Skulker Moss and a Hardened Tumor to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity.",d="According to Berard's Journal the moss from Lake Skulkers and Creepers might prove useful for our quest to brew a new plague.  Those beasts dwell on the islands in Lake Lordamere to the east.\n\nHe also mentions a very rare Hardened Tumor that he discovered on a Vile Fin murloc.  Apparently the tumor is so rare Berard was only able to obtain one.\n\nCollect samples of the moss as well as the rare hardened tumor and take them to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity.",p="What brings you back to the Undercity, $N?",c="Such a blow to the Royal Apothecary Society to lose Berard.  But through your hard work and Apothecary Renferrel's diligent research Berard's studies will still be useful to The Dark Lady's plight.\n\nWe are on the cusp of something great here, $N.  If you were not so skilled in the ways of combat I would try to recruit you for membership in the Society."},
[493]={t="Journey to Hillsbrad Foothills",o="Deliver Apothecary Renferrel's findings to Apothecary Lydon in the town of Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills.",d="The Royal Apothecary Society is under extreme pressure from the Dark Lady to develop a New Plague.  We are working diligently and have made much progress.  It is our belief that the success will be achieved much faster if we share information amongst the Society.\n\nFor that reason I want you to deliver my latest findings to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill, a small town nestled in the Hillsbrad Foothills.  The journey will be a long one.\n\nHead south and stick to the roads.  Follow the signs closely!",p="You have something for me?",c="Ah, most excellent.  Apothecary Renferrel has my utmost respect.  I am anxious to study his work."},
[494]={t="Time To Strike",o="Travel to Tarren Mill to deliver Deathstalker Lesh's message to High Executor Darthalia.",d="Be silent and pay attention, $C.\n\nI was sent to this position in order to survey the town of Hillsbrad.  My mission is one of reconnaissance.  It is imperative that you send word to High Executor Darthalia in Tarren Mill at once.  Let her know that I, Deathstalker Lesh, send the following message:\n\n\"The raven's cry from the west doth beckon.\"\n\nFollow the road to the east and pay close attention to the signs.  Now, hurry!  Off you go to Tarren Mill, and with urgency I might add!",c="The raven's cry from the west doth beckon?\n\nSuperb news!  Hillsbrad is ripe for attack.  We can carry out our plan of destruction now.  Varimathras will be pleased."},
[496]={t="Elixir of Suffering",o="Apothecary Lydon of Tarren Mill wants 10 Gray Bear Tongues and some Creeper Ichor.",d="Ah, another wretched day in Tarren Mill.  All of this clean air puts me in such a foul mood, $N.\n\nThe sooner we can plague the humans here, the better.  I've been conducting intense studies on possible killing agents to use in my concoctions but I haven't the time to collect them all.\n\nIf you want to make yourself of use, procure the following items for me:  10 Gray Bear Tongues and the very rare and hard to find, Creeper Ichor.  You'll find both bears and creepers just outside of Tarren Mill."},
[527]={t="Battle of Hillsbrad",o="Kill 6 Hillsbrad Farmhands, 6 Hillsbrad Farmers, Farmer Ray and Farmer Getz and report back to Darthalia in Tarren Mill.",d="Stand at attention while addressing me, $C.\n\nI am under direct command of Varimathras.  We are to quell the human infestation until our apothecaries can develop the new plague.\n\nOur information leads us to believe that the town of Hillsbrad is vulnerable to attack.  Your first assignment is aimed at disrupting their food supply and infrastructure.\n\nTravel west.  Raid the northernmost farms of Hillsbrad Fields.  Make sure that the landowners, Farmer Ray and Farmer Getz, are executed as well."},
[744]={t="Preparation for Ceremony",o="Collect 6 Azure Feathers and 6 Bronze Feathers, and bring them to Eyahn Eagletalon in Thunder Bluff.",d="$N, my brother soon stands before Chief Bloodhoof, and it is my honor to make his headdress for him.\n\nI want to ask a favor of you while I finish tanning these leather straps. There is not time for me to find enough feathers, and I was wondering, would you gather more for me?\n\nYou can find feathers of the correct size from the harpies residing far to the north and northwest of Thunder Bluff. I need only 6 azure and 6 bronze feathers to complete the design."},
[786]={t="Thwarting Kolkar Aggression",o="Lar Prowltusk outside of Sen'jin Village wants you to destroy the 3 sets of Attack Plans held within Kolkar Crag.",d="Lower your voice, $C. The Kolkar centaurs lie just over the ridge to the west in Kolkar Crag.\n\nLast night while they were raiding, I snuck into their village and discovered that the dirty beasts have a three-tiered attack planned on the trolls and orcs of Durotar.\n\nWe mustn't let their invasion come to fruition. Perhaps you can muster the might needed to infiltrate Kolkar Crag and destroy their attack plans.\n\nLast I saw, they had divided them up amongst three of their leaders."},
[816]={t="Lost But Not Forgotten",o="Bring a sign of Kron's fate to Misha Tor'kren at the farmstead northwest of Razor Hill.",d="$N, please, can you help me? My son Kron went hunting days ago, and he still hasn't returned. He went west towards the Barrens to hunt crocolisks along Southfury River. I fear the worst.\n\nAs strong as he was, his stubborn pride has always drawn him into trouble. I warned him that the crocolisks were powerful and vicious. He grew angry and stormed off.\n\nIf you can't find him, at least bring me a sign of his fate... even if you have to open up the stomach of every crocolisk along the Southfury's banks."},
[819]={t="Chen's Empty Keg",o="Find someone who knows about Chen's Empty Keg.",d="A small placard on one of the ends of the keg says,\n\n\"Chen Stormstout-\n\nMay your spirit be raised and always raise your spirits.\"",p="Yes?",c="Well, I'll be...\n\nThis was one of Chen Stormstout's kegs. He traveled with Rexxar a long time ago. I haven't seen or heard about him in a kodo's age. I appreciate you bringing this to me, $N."},
[821]={t="Chen's Empty Keg",o="Bring 5 Savannah Lion Tusks, 5 Plainstrider Kidneys, and 1 Thunder Lizard Horn to Brewmaster Drohn in Ratchet.",d="Would you like a taste of Chen's namesake? Ahh, the stormstout is a mighty brew. Chen taught the recipe to my mentor, and my mentor passed it on to me. I'll need you to get me a few things, but I can tell you this: the kick is worth it.\n\nBring me 5 savannah lion tusks from any savannah lion, 5 plainstrider kidneys from any plainstrider, and 1 thunder lizard horn from any species of thunder lizard. That should do the trick nicely.\n\nYou can find these ingredients throughout the Barrens.",p="How's the search going?",c="Haha... I never thought I'd make more of this stuff ever again.\n\nYou've stirred in me a great sense of nostalgia, $N. Kind of reminds me of the last time I made a batch of trogg brew. Thank you. The memories warm my stomach."},
[822]={t="Chen's Empty Keg",o="Bring 5 Lightning Glands, 1 Thunderhawk Saliva Gland and 1 Kodo Liver to Brewmaster Drohn in Ratchet.",d="Good stuff, that stormstout, huh?\n\nI have another recipe that I learned from Chen. Would you be interested? It won't take long to make, and it might be useful if you plan on adventuring some more.\n\nBring me 5 lightning glands from any stormhide, 1 thunderhawk saliva gland from greater thunderhawks, and a kodo liver from any of the Barrens' kodos.\n\nLike I said, this stuff has kick; it's the trogg brew that I mentioned to you before.",p="You working hard at finding those ingredients, $N?",c="Haha! I knew you couldn't resist some of this brew. Come back again anytime you want some more, $N. Just bring me more of the ingredients I had you collect."},
[844]={t="Plainstrider Menace",o="Collect 7 Plainstrider Beaks and return them to Sergra Darkthorn in the Crossroads.",d="Your first prey will be easy.\n\nThe plainstriders to the east have been harassing our food supplies and have become a nuisance.\n\nPut down the plainstriders and return to me with their beaks.",p="Have you collected the plainstrider beaks?",c="Very good, $N.  With the plainstriders gone we'll have an easier time keeping our supply chains intact.  And I hope you learned a few tricks out there in the Barrens, for your next prey has a little more fire in its blood than the plainstriders..."},
[845]={t="The Zhevra",o="Slay Zhevra Runners to collect 4 Zhevra Hooves for Sergra Darkthorn in the Crossroads.",d="The zhevra, although not the fiercest beast in the Barrens, are a shade tougher than the plainstriders.  Don't worry -- we'll send you against bigger prey in good time, but for now your teeth could use a little more cutting.\n\nHunt the zhevra to the north and south, and collect their hooves.  Bring them to me and perhaps we'll next send you against something tougher.",p="How many zhevra have you slain?",c="Not bad, $N.  Those zhevra hold a lot of strength in their legs.  A sharp kick from them can knock even a tauren on its haunches!\n\nIt looks like you have some strength in you too.  Are you ready for a real challenge?"},
[848]={t="Fungal Spores",o="Bring 4 Fungal Spores to Apothecary Helbrim at the Crossroads.",d="The oases of the Barrens hide a mystery.  Life energy flows from their waters, invigorating the plants and beasts that drink it.\n\nInvigorating, and altering.\n\nThere is a mushroom that grows near these oases.  Its spores hold properties that we, the apothecaries of Lordaeron, find useful.\n\nBring me these spores and you will earn our gratitude.",p="Do you have the spores, $N?  There is a concoction I must send to my associate in Thunder Bluff, which requires the spores...",c="Ah, yes.  These are good specimens.  Potent.\n\nI am Forsaken, and we honor our contracts.  Here is your reward, $N."},
[853]={t="Apothecary Zamah",o="Bring the Rendered Spores to Apothecary Zamah in Thunder Bluff, before the time limit is up.",d="I have rendered the spores you gave me into an emulsion.  I must now send it to my associate, Apothecary Zamah.  If you were to carry this to her, she can offer you something from our stores of alchemical goods.\n\nShe is in the Pools of Vision, a cave beneath the shamans of Thunder Bluff.  The path to this cave is well hidden, but you may find it on the Spirit Rise bluff.\n\nDo hurry.  This emulsion will maintain its potency for only a short time, and must be resealed and processed before then.",p="You have something from Apothecary Helbrim?",c="Ah, the spores from the Barrens that Helbrim was gathering.  He garnered your aid in delivering them?  Good.\n\nAnd the emulsion is still potent, so you must have wasted no time in the delivery.  Well done, $C."},
[858]={t="Ignition",o="Get the Ignition Key and bring it to Wizzlecrank.",d="I don't suppose Sputtervalve sent you? I'm in a bind here. I hopped in without realizing that I need a key to unlock the shredder's movement column. One of the other shredder operators asked me if everything was okay, and I panicked! Instead of telling him that I was missing my key, I told him there was some sort of mechanical problem.\n\nWe need to get out of here on the double! Go up to the control room at the top of the derrick, the supervisor should have a key for this shredder.\n\nHelp me out here!",p="Quick, we need to get out of here before someone gets suspicious!",c="Yep, this looks like the right key. Let me just make sure I know how to work this thing...\n\nHmm... rotation control... This regulates speed and stability... fine arm movement control. Just look at this! I can't believe the Venture Company could design something this much better than ours. I've got to get this back to Ratchet!"},
[862]={t="Dig Rat Stew",o="Bring 8 Dig Rats to Grub east of the Crossroads.",d="A $C like you must get pretty hungry out here in The Barrens. Me, I'm starving all day long.\n\nTell you what, I'll fix you up a nice stew. Just need a few dig rats.\n\nSeems those filthy dwarves at Bael Modan are overrun with everyone's favorite feast. Now head on down south to Bael Modan and bring me back some dig rats.\n\nYou can't call yourself a seasoned adventurer until you've spent some time killing rats! Haw!"},
[863]={t="The Escape",o="Protect Wizzlecrank and the stolen goblin shredder on the way to Sputtervalve in Ratchet.",d="I suppose I'll learn as we go... Couldn't be too hard. Just some buttons here, and a lever or two... Well, are you ready to go?",c="Hopefully we'll be able to get something of value from the wrecked shredder prototype... my time's running out! I'll dispatch a salvage team to Wizzlecrank's location on the double.\n\nOh, let me give you something for your trouble, too."},
[865]={t="Raptor Horns",o="Gather 5 Intact Raptor Horns from Sunscale Scytheclaws, and bring them to Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.",d="The raptors of the Barrens are smarter than raptors in other lands.  And I think all that smarts is hiding in their horns!  If so, then I could grind their horns into powder and use it to make \"smart drinks.\"  I could sell them for a fortune!!!\n\nAnd you can help me.  Find me intact raptor horns from sunscale scytheclaws.  They roam in the southern Barrens, and in the northern Barrens near the border of Ashenvale Forest.",p="Did you get the horns, $N?  Those things are going to make me a fortune!",c="Great, you got them!  Now I just need to ground them down and mix them with some wine, and..."},
[866]={t="Root Samples",o="Bring 8 Root Samples to Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.",d="The herbs of the Barrens are not quite like herbs in other lands.  Their properties are mostly the same, but the oasis water here alters the plants; they are just slightly different.\n\nI want to study those differences... to see if they're exploitable!\n\nIf you are skilled in herbalism, then gather root samples off the herbs you find in the Barrens.  Bring back these samples so that I may compare them with herbs from other regions.",p="Hello, $N.  Did you get those root samples?",c="Yes yes, these are very nice!  I will grow specimens from these roots and study them.  I hope to find new properties from them.  Hidden, valuable properties...!\n\nAnd don't worry -- if I do then you'll be the first to know.  Because I'll need someone to gather more!"},
[867]={t="Harpy Raiders",o="Collect 8 Witchwing talons.\n\nReturn them to Darsok Swiftdagger at the Crossroads.",d="The blasted harpies have been ravaging our caravan supplies for too long. It's time we slit a few of their throats and diminished their numbers.\n\nI've been snooping around their nests and figured out who leads who. The most devastating attack will destroy a good section of their lower chain of command and then we can work our way to the top.\n\nI'll start you off slow, take out Witchwing Harpies and Witchwing Roguefeathers in the Northwest and bring me 8 Witchwing talons. That should be a good start...",p="Cut up enough of them yet? Keep slicing and taking trophies. I want 8 Witchwing talons.",c="Oh, these are nice. Real nice... Good job, $N. I look forward to seeing more of your work in the future."},
[869]={t="Raptor Thieves",o="Bring 12 Raptor Heads to Gazrog at the Crossroads.",d="Not long ago, a shipment of silver was stolen from our guard tower.  It was meant as payroll to the Crossroads' guards, and we want that silver back.\n\nThe strange thing is... we caught one of the thieves on the night of the theft.  And... it was a raptor!  Unbelievable!\n\nI don't know what raptors would want with silver.  But I don't care -- I want the raptors dead so they won't steal from us again!\n\nHunt raptors in the Barrens.  Collect for me their heads!",p="Do you have those heads, $N?",c="You got rid of the raptors!\n\nThank you, $N.  You are a shaman of worth."},
[870]={t="The Forgotten Pools",o="Report back to Tonga Runetotem with your findings.",d="Long ago, the Barrens was a lush place, teeming with life.  But war and cataclysm raged across the land, scorching it and leaving a dry husk.  Such is the way of things, and it saddens my heart.\n\nBut within the past few years, new oases have formed in the Barrens, and life stirs.  And deep down, we druids sense a power leaking its way to the surface.\n\nWe must find its source.  Travel to the Forgotten Pools, northwest of the Crossroads.  Search its waters for a source of power, then return here.",c="You found a fissure in the earth, with gases bubbling from it?  Strange.  This may be an answer to our questions, but we cannot yet be sure.\n\nBut it is a clue.  And I am grateful that you found it."},
[871]={t="Disrupt the Attacks",o="Of the Razormane tribe, kill 8 Water Seekers, 8 Thornweavers and 3 Hunters, and then return to Thork in the Crossroads.",d="All the quilboars are our enemies, $N. Some just prove to be more of a nuisance than others.\n\nThe Razormane tribe has been attacking our supply lines from Durotar, causing us no end of annoyance. I have scouts seeking the leader of these raids, but until then, any losses you can inflict on the filthy pig men would aid us.\n\nStart in the northeast towards Durotar. You can always tell their dens from the huge thorny vines that come up from the earth. Seek them out, and slay them."},
[875]={t="Harpy Lieutenants",o="Collect 6 Harpy Lieutenant Rings from Witchwing Slayers and return them to Darsok Swiftdagger at the Crossroads.",d="Hahaha, $N. Back for more? Good, I like to hear that.\n\nThis time I want you to assassinate some of the harpy lieutenants in the Dry Hills. Only Witchwing Slayers can be lieutenants, and you can tell them apart by the rings they carry. They are a nasty bunch, but they lead some of the underlings in that area. Taking out 6 of them will be a decisive strike against their matriarchy.\n\nMake sure they die painfully, $N. We want those harpy wenches to know the idiocy of picking fights with the Horde.",p="Do you have 6 Harpy Lieutenant Rings yet? Justice must be dealt to them for their vicious attacks on the Horde.",c="Excellent work my friend. I think you'll go far within the Horde."},
[876]={t="Serena Bloodfeather",o="Slay Serena Bloodfeather and return her head to Darsok Swiftdagger at the Crossroads.",d="You did so well with the lieutenants and underlings that I'd like you to do one last thing for me.\n\nSerena Bloodfeather is the sister of a harpy named Bloodfeather who was slain by Rexxar quite a while ago. Apparently, these attacks on the Horde caravans are revenge for her sister's death.\n\nI need you to slit her throat and bring me back her head. I want to place it on the next caravan we send out... Give those harpies something to think about.",p="You're not getting anything until I see Serena's head.",c="HA! Well done, $N! Very well done... I wasn't sure you were up to the task, but you've proved yourself quite the cut-throat. Thank you again for helping us suppress the Harpy epidemic. Here is your reward, use it well."},
[877]={t="The Stagnant Oasis",o="Return to Tonga at The Crossroads, after investigating the Stagnant Oasis.",d="Like the one you found at the Forgotten Pools, there may be fissures at the other oases in the Barrens.  If so, then perhaps the fissures are the oases' source of life.\n\nWe must test this.\n\nHere, take these seeds.  They are dead and infertile, but take them to the Stagnant Oasis to the southeast.  If there is a fissure there, then place the seeds within it...and observe.",c="Your findings are amazing!  The seeds I gave you were dried, and dead.  Whatever rests under these oases can create life from nothing!\n\nWe must study this more..."},
[880]={t="Altered Beings",o="Bring 8 Altered Snapjaw Shells to Tonga Runetotem at the Crossroads.",d="Your findings are incredible, $N.  These oases hold properties that must come from an outside source.  Or perhaps an inside one.\n\nI want to know how these fissures are affecting the beasts who drink from the oases' water.\n\nHunt oasis snapjaws at the Lushwater and Stagnant Oases.  Bring me their shells so I may examine them.",p="How goes your collection?  Did you get the shells?",c="Thank you, $N.  Studying the beasts of an area can tell much about the area itself.  We shall see what tale these shells tell.\n\nPlease accept my gratitude for your aid ... and perhaps you can use these coins.  I find that I do not need them."},
[881]={t="Echeyakee",o="Bring Echeyakee's Hide to Sergra Darkthorn at the Crossroads.",d="Whitemist, Echeyakee in the Tauren tongue, is the king of the savannah cats.  He hunts with such stealth, they say he's like a thin, white mist on the earth.  And he kills so fast his prey have no time for fear, or pain.\n\nThe Tauren say he is both mercy and death.\n\nYou will learn if that's true, for I now set you on the path to hunt Echeyakee.  His lair is northeast of the Crossroads, among the bones of giant Kodo\n\nGo.  Blow this horn when you reach his lair.  Blow the horn, and he will come.",p="The great cat calls to you, $N.",c="You've beaten Echeyakee, and though his days of hunting are over... his spirit is with you.  He will show you the strength found in subtlety, and the honor in mercy.\n\nYour path is still long, $C.  Let's hope you stride it well."},
[882]={t="Ishamuhale",o="Bring Ishamuhale's Fang to Jorn at Camp Taurajo.",d="Ishamuhale, Speartooth, is the fiercest sunscale raptor of the Barrens.  He does not hunt for sport, nor for food.  He hunts because hunting is his passion.  He kills because it is his nature to kill.\n\nAnd you will learn of his nature, $N, for your path now follows the taloned tracks of Ishamuhale.\n\nBegin the hunt.  Slay his favorite prey, a zhevra, then bring its carcass to the dead tree northwest of Ratchet.  Ishamuhale will smell the carcass and be drawn to it.\n\nBe ready when he comes."},
[883]={t="Lakota'mani",o="Bring the Hoof of Lakota'mani to Jorn at Camp Taurajo.",d="The Hoof of Lakota'mani is a symbol of the strength of the great kodo.",p="$N, when you approached I saw a new power in your stride.  Tell me -- has your spirit met with the great Lakota'mani?",c="Lakota'mani is called \"Earthshaker\" in our language, and his steps are like gathered thunder.  He is with you now, and his courage mingles with yours.  Together there is no conflict you cannot face.\n\nWalk tall, $N.  Walk tall, Earthshaker."},
[884]={t="Owatanka",o="Bring Owatanka's Tailspike to Jorn at Camp Taurajo.",d="When touched, sparks fly from the tailspike of Owatanka.",p="$N, there is a new power behind your eyes!  You have met with the mighty Owatanka, have you not?",c="The thunder lizard Owatanka is called \"Bluebolt\" by the tauren, for within him resides a speed that belies his size.  It is said that lightning struck Bluebolt long ago and, fed from the sky's rage, the great beast's energy is without limit.\n\nMay his energy flow through you, $N.  For you now keep pace with Owatanka."},
[886]={t="The Barrens Oases",o="Speak with Tonga Runetotem at the Crossroads.",d="The druids of Thunder Bluff sense a strange power leaking into the Barrens, east of Mulgore.\n\nTonga Runetotem was sent to discover the source of this power, but we fear he will need aid.\n\nTravel to the Barrens and speak with Tonga.  He will be at the Crossroads.  To reach there, take the road east out of Bloodhoof village.  Enter the Barrens, then turn north when the road forks.  Continue north and  you will find the Crossroads.\n\nAnd do not leave the road, $N, for the Barrens is a harsh land.",c="My brethren in Thunder Bluff were wise to send you, young $C.  For the mystery of the Barrens is one that I alone cannot unravel.\n\nWith your aid, let us hope we can find answers to our questions."},
[887]={t="Southsea Freebooters",o="Kill 12 Southsea Brigands and 6 Southsea Cannoneers for Gazlowe in Ratchet.",d="I sure wish Vice Admiral Grezzlik did a better job of keeping the seas safe for our trading vessels. With all the gold the trade princes have poured into the Trade Fleets, it ticks me off to see so many pirates running willy-nilly, raiding my ships and stealing my goods!\n\nI heard that the Southsea Freebooters have set up a camp just south of here. They've been a real thorn in my side and if Grezzlik won't take care of them, well, maybe you can help me get rid of them."},
[891]={t="The Guns of Northwatch",o="Captain Thalo'thas Brightsun of Ratchet wants you to collect 10 Theramore Medals and slay Captain Fairmount, Cannoneer Whessan and Cannoneer Smythe.",d="Yet another ship from my fleet has been lost to those overzealous humans at Northwatch Hold!\n\nThose bastards must be dealt with. Their paranoia has them in a state of frenzy. Trigger happy, reckless louts are shooting at anything in their sights.\n\nTravel south along the Merchant Coast to the Hold and lay siege to their forces. Bring me the medals of their soldiers as proof. And for the love of my fleet, slay Captain Fairmount and her overzealous cannoneers!"},
[894]={t="Samophlange",o="Access the control console at the Venture Company research site.",d="The Venture Company set up a small research facility far to the north of here, southwest of the Sludge Fen. I don't know very much about what they're doing, but did manage to discover that they're experimenting with something called a \"samophlange\".\n\nNow what the heck is a samophlange? Well, whatever it is, I want to examine it, so I need someone to go get it.\n\nI obtained a copy of their control system operating manual, you should be able to figure out how to disengage the samophlange from it.",c="A variety of buttons, levers and blinking lights are somewhat erratically arrayed on the face of the control console. A small gauge indicates that the apparatus is currently operating within optimal levels, and indicates that control valves one through three are currently open. There is a small keyhole set into the lower right side of the control panel."},
[895]={t="WANTED: Baron Longshore",o="Bring the head of Baron Longshore to Gazlowe in Ratchet.",d="WANTED!\n\nBaron Longshore, Captain of the Heedless\n\nCaptain Longshore of Gilneas leads vessels of the Southsea Freebooters, and is wanted on charges of piracy. Remains must be in identifiable condition!\n\n-- Gazlowe"},
[896]={t="Miner's Fortune",o="Retrieve the Cats Eye Emerald from one of the Venture Co. Overseers or Enforcers for Wharfmaster Dizzywig at Ratchet.",d="Being Wharfmaster of a busy port like Ratchet, I keep my finger on the pulse of information. I know all about the exchange of goods and money between here and Booty Bay.\n\nThe latest bit of news I've heard is about the Venture Company's Boulder Lode mine northeast of the Sludge Fen. One of the miners discovered an emerald the size of your fist. I know a few buyers who'd be interested in getting their hands on something like that, and I'd be willing to go half and half on its sale.",p="If only we knew which one of the miners had found the emerald, it'd be a walk in the park...",c="Look at the size of that thing, $N! We're going to be rich! Let's see, according to the rates I've seen on gems going into Undermine, I should be able to figure out your cut--fifty percent, don't worry!\n\nNow let's see... I think this should do about right. Pleasure doing business with you, $N."},
[899]={t="Consumed by Hatred",o="Bring 60 Bristleback Quilboar Tusks to Mankrik at the Crossroads.",d="Perhaps you know the pain of uncertainty, perhaps not, $C. But know this: I stand here every day, from the sun's rising till its decline, scouring the horizon for more of those monsters. I've killed every pig man I've come across since, but my thirst for their blood is far from quenched. Perhaps instead of heading north to the Crossroads I should have headed to Taurajo.\n\nYou, $C--you  could help me.\n\nKill them. Kill as many as you can. Bring me their tusks, and we will celebrate their deaths together."},
[900]={t="Samophlange",o="Close off the Fuel Control Valve, the Regulator Valve and the Main Control Valve then use the control console again.",d="The three control valves are currently opened. The various readings on the control panel lead you to presume that they must be shut off before the apparatus can be shut off.",c="The lights indicating the three control valves dim as they are shut off. Green lights slowly fade into yellow, and the switch controlling the apparatus is now moveable, with the valves closed, it can be turned off."},
[901]={t="Samophlange",o="Get the Console Key from Tinkerer Sniggles to use on the control console.",d="With the apparatus deactivated, the control panel can be opened up and the samophlange removed from the console. With everything else in place, all that is left is to acquire the key to unlock the console.",p="The console lights are dimmed and the gauges and dials all read at their zero positions, everything idling.",c="Turning the key in the lock, the control console unlocks. A red light at the top of the console turns off and all power drains from the terminal."},
[902]={t="Samophlange",o="Return the Samophlange to Sputtervalve in Ratchet.",d="Pulling open the face of the control console reveals a dense jumble of wires, tubing and other strange mechanical objects--most of which seem to serve no practical purpose. Pushing them aside and digging deeper into the console, you find the samophlange. A tug removes it from its housing.",p="Oh, you're back, $N! Do you have the samophlange?",c="This is... er... interesting... yes. I'll have it sent along to the Tinkers' Union headquarters in Undermine. I'm sure after some careful dissection and research, they'll be able to make some sense of it.\n\nBut, perhaps I'll have a little look myself first..."},
[903]={t="Prowlers of the Barrens",o="Collect 7 Prowler Claws from Savannah Prowlers for Sergra Darkthorn in the Crossroads.",d="Now it's time to go after something that really bites.  The prowlers of the Barrens are a tough breed.  Tough, resourceful, sly... and deadly.  You'll find them among the tall grasses.  You'll find many to the southwest of the Crossroads.\n\nBe wary as you hunt them, $N, or you may find yourself no longer the predator, but instead the prey.",p="How goes your hunt, $N?  Have you found the prowlers?",c="Ah, I see you've been busy, lurking in the grasses and hunting prowlers.  Do you think, then, it is time to face a champion among them?"},
[905]={t="The Angry Scytheclaws",o="Kill Sunscale raptors and collect their feathers. Use the feathers on the 3 Scytheclaw nests. Return to Sergra Darkthorn in the Crossroads.",d="Now, $N, the hunt deepens.  Now you must defeat your prey, and then find your way to its lair.\n\nHunt the sunscale raptors to the south.  Slay them and remove the feathers they wear.  Place the feathers on the scytheclaw nests southwest of the Stagnant Oasis. Show their brethren you do not fear them!",c="So you've been to the nests and placed the feathers of your prey within them.  That took a fair portion of courage, no doubt about it.\n\nDo you feel a little tougher, $N?  Because you look tougher now then when you first came here.  I guess the Barrens is doing its job."},
[914]={t="Leaders of the Fang",o="Bring the Gems of Cobrahn, Anacondra, Pythas and Serpentis to Nara Wildmane in Thunder Bluff.",d="The druids in the Wailing Caverns, the Druids of the Fang, are an aberration.  They were part of an order of noble druids whose plan was to heal the Barrens, but now seek to remake that land to match their own, twisted dreams.\n\nThe Druids of the Fang have four leaders, and each possesses a dream gem.  Even now their faces haunt me!  Defeat the leaders and bring me their gems, and the Barrens may again know peace.\n\nGo, $N.  You will find them lurking deep within the Wailing Caverns.",p="Memories of my nightmares haunt me, $N.  Have you defeated the leaders of the fang and acquired their gems?",c="You have done it, $N.  You killed the leaders of the Druids of the Fang.  My dreams are now free of their wicked faces, and you have helped save the Barrens from a cursed future.\n\nI thank you, $N.  I thank you for myself, for the druids of Thunder Bluff, and for the land."},
[959]={t="Trouble at the Docks",o="Crane Operator Bigglefuzz in Ratchet wants you to retrieve the bottle of 99-Year-Old Port from Mad Magglish who is hiding in the Wailing Caverns.",d="Oops!\n\nHad a little mishap, as you can see! The morning cargo shipment from Booty Bay was huge. Huge I say! Never seen so many crates. Well, I was trying to expedite things so I started unloading a bit more than I could handle. That's when everything came tumbling down.\n\nBefore I knew what was going on, I saw that menace, Mad Magglish, go running off with a bottle of 99-year-old port. Chased him all the way to Wailing Caverns. No way I was going in there.\n\nMaybe you're brave enough to find him?",p="The dockmaster has been on my case ever since Mad Magglish made off with that 99-year-old port. I guess that bottle was intended as a gift for Gazlowe from none other than Baron Revilgaz himself.\n\nIf you're brave enough and patient enough to seek out Mad Magglish and get that port back, I'll see to it you get a nice reward.",c="Superb! And just as I was about to lose my job too! I will see to it that Gazlowe gets this gift immediately.\n\nThank you, $N. Nicely done, I say!"},
[962]={t="Serpentbloom",o="Apothecary Zamah in Thunder Bluff wants you to collect 10 Serpentbloom.",d="The Royal Apothecary Society, based in the great Undercity of Lordaeron, has sent me here for a very specific service, $N. Perhaps you wish to aid me, and in turn The Dark Lady in our efforts to advance the Forsaken.\n\nRecently I studied a rare specimen of flora named Serpentbloom. I believe in greater quantities this herb has great potential.\n\nUnfortunately Serpentbloom can only be found in the darkest recesses of the Wailing Caverns, a dangerous cave system located in the Barrens.",p="I am eager to see if you can gather enough Serpentbloom from the Wailing Caverns. I've sent many to do my bidding but none have returned.",c="Ah, splendid specimens. You have done well, $N."},
[972]={t="Water Sapta",c="Take the water sapta and find the corrupted pool of water in Silverpine, $N. I have great faith in your abilities."},
[1058]={t="Jin'Zil's Forest Magic",o="Witch Doctor Jin'Zil at Malaka'jin wants 5 portions of Stonetalon Sap, 5 Twilight Whiskers, 30 Courser Eyes and a Fey Dragon Scale.",d="So excited I am!\n\nThree little cages for three little elves! But what shall we do with our lovely tree-hugging friends? Why, let's give them a taste of... what do they call it... forest magic!\n\nI'll need a good mess of Stonetalon sap. From those horrid felines, bring me some twilight whiskers. This calls for plenty of courser eyes, of course -- can never have enough eyes. Oh, and lest we forget, a precious scale from a fey dragon.\n\nHurry to Stonetalon Peak, $N, so I can brew some forest magic!"},
[1060]={t="Letter to Jin'Zil",o="Deliver Darsok's letter to Jin'Zil within his cave in Malaka'Jin, in Stonetalon.",d="You've done so well for me, $N. You're a regular lucky rabbit's foot and there's something I want you to see.\n\nThe harpies are not from around the Barrens. They come from a place called Stonetalon, far to the northwest of here. Though it is probably a dangerous place for you, I need this letter delivered to an old friend of mine who lives there, a witch doctor by the name of Jin'Zil.\n\nHe'll be happy to know that Serena Bloodfeather is dead, and I think you'll find Stonetalon an interesting place.",p="You seem a shady character. You have something for me to see?",c="Ahh, a letter from Darsok. I have not heard from him in many years.\n\nSo the last of the Bloodfeathers are dead, eh? That is good news, I can remember when my friend Rokhan went with that crazy mok'nathal to kill her older sister. Ah, to be young again, like you."},
[1061]={t="The Spirits of Stonetalon",o="Speak with Seereth Stonebreak in the Stonetalon Mountains.",d="The spirits of the Stonetalon Mountains are angered, for goblins and their servants are plundering and burning the land.  So the land has cried out, and those who listen for such things... have heard.\n\nSeereth Stonebreak, a promising shaman of the Horde, was sent to Stonetalon.  She reports massive deforestation at the hands of the goblins, and requests aid.\n\nMeet Seereth in Stonetalon.  To reach her, follow the road west of the Barrens' Crossroads.  She is camped near the Greatwood Vale.",c="Ah, a shaman.  Very good.  We will need your skills to deal with these plunderers!"},
[1062]={t="Goblin Invaders",o="Kill 15 Venture Co. Loggers, then return to Seereth Stonebreak on the border of Stonetalon and the Barrens.",d="The goblin-run Venture Company moved into the Stonetalon Mountains, chopping down trees and burning huge stretches of forest.  The spirits of this place are nearly blind with pain and rage.  We must stop the Venture Company!\n\nHead northwest, beyond the Greatwood Vale and into the Windshear Crag.  You will find the goblins and their servants at work -- show them the Horde will not allow the exploitation of Stonetalon.  Show them in the language they best understand...\n\nViolence.",c="Bravely done, $N.\n\nWe may ultimately need the wisdom of tauren elders to calm the spirits of Stonetalon, but...\n\nRidding the Venture Company of its personnel is a good first move against them."},
[1063]={t="The Elder Crone",o="Speak with Magatha in Thunder Bluff.",d="To truly tend the spirits of Stonetalon we must consult the tauren elders.\n\nI do not know many of their leaders' names, but I do know of one: Magatha.  I have heard that she is very old, and she knows much.  If anyone can marshal spiritual aid from the tauren, it is she.\n\nMagatha resides in the tauren capital of Thunder Bluff, on Elder Rise -- the city's northeastern bluff.  Speak with Magatha, and tell her of the peril of Stonetalon Mountains.",c="I bid you greetings.  You are here seeking counsel?"},
[1064]={t="Forsaken Aid",o="Speak with Apothecary Zamah in the Pools of Vision in Thunder Bluff.",d="The tauren have a bond with the land, and it pains me to hear of Stonetalon's plight.  But I fear that to heal the land, we must first remove the disease upon it.\n\nIs it not fortunate, then, that the Forsaken are allied with us?  They know much of disease.  I believe they can aid us, and by doing so they will strengthen the trust between our people.\n\nSpeak with Apothecary Zamah.  She is a scholar and an emissary of the Forsaken.  You will find her in the Pools of Vision below the Spirit Rise.",c="Magatha sent word of your coming, $N.  Although my heart beats no longer, I still feel sorrow for the spirits of Stonetalon.\n\nThe Forsaken are eager to offer what help we can."},
[1065]={t="Journey to Tarren Mill",o="Bring Zamah's Note to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.",d="To rid Stonetalon of the Venture Company, we must take extreme measures.  Extreme, but without bloodshed.\n\nA colleague of mine may have just the tool we need.  His name is Lydon; he dwells in the town of Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills, in the distant land of Lordaeron.\n\nTo reach Hillsbrad, travel by zeppelin to our capital, the Undercity.  Then go north to Tirisfal Glades, southwest to Silverpine, and south to Hillsbrad.\n\nSeek Lydon and bring him this note.  It details our needs to him."},
[1068]={t="Shredding Machines",o="Kill the shredders XT:4 and XT:9, then return to Seereth Stonebreak at the border of the Stonetalon Mountains and the Barrens.",d="There is a relation to the spiritual magic of shamans and the natural magic of druids.  This is why we shamans can hear the plea of the spirits of Stonetalon.  Many of their whisperings are lost to me, but one message, one vision, is clear...\n\nI saw a vision of two man-shaped machines in Windshear Crag, northwest of Greatwood Vale, felling trees with impossible speed.  These metal beasts must be stopped!\n\nIn my vision, the machines were marked with strange symbols:\n\nXT:4 and XT:9.",c="The destruction of the machines XT:4 and XT:9 have soothed many of the spirits of Stonetalon, $N.  With their loss, let us hope the Venture Company will remove itself from these mountains.\n\nFor if they do not, then I fear the atrocities this place has suffered will pale to what lies ahead."},
[1069]={t="Deepmoss Spider Eggs",o="Bring 15 Deepmoss Eggs to Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.",d="Spider egg omelettes are a new fad in Booty Bay!  The problem is... Booty Bay's got no eggs.\n\nI smell an opportunity!\n\nIn Windshear Crag and Sishir Canyon, in the Stonetalon Mountains to the northwest, lives the deepmoss spider.  Bring me its eggs and I'll pay a bundle!\n\nIn Windshear Crag, the eggs will be clustered under what trees remain.\n\nIn Sishir Canyon... well, if you have a weak stomach then maybe you should just collect the eggs at Windshear Crag...",p="Did you get the eggs, $N?  I already made a shipping deal with Wharfmaster Dizzywig!",c="You got them!  Thank you!\n\nI'll have these sent to Dizzywig and get them shipped to Booty Bay.  I can already taste the profits!\n\nHere is your cut, $N.  I couldn't have made this deal without you."},
[1087]={t="Cenarius' Legacy",o="Kill 4 Sons of Cenarius, 4 Daughters of Cenarius and 4 Cenarion Botanists for Braelyn Firehand near Sun Rock Retreat.",d="You cannot imagine the hatred I possess for this wretched land. The ilk of Cenarius and the kaldorei druids at the peak employ their pathetic powers to stifle the flow of magic, even so far south of their pathetic holdings... their beloved forests.\n\nWould that I could return to Jaedenar and exult in the flow of magic, but my master will not allow me to return until my work is done.\n\nI have no doubt you love the night elves and their allies as little as I. Aid me, and both our ends might be satisfied."},
[1090]={t="Gerenzo's Orders",o="Get the mysterious ore from Piznik after he finishes mining it.",d="You know, I was once the second most important person here at this site. That all changed when Gerenzo took over. Fired my boss, Ziz Fizziks, and sent me down to work in the mines. Ziz told me to stay here and gather information, though. His new boss will pay us well if we can find out what Gerenzo's plans are.\n\nAnyways, what I do know is that Gerenzo has ordered large amounts of this gold-green ore to be mined. I can get you a sample to bring to Ziz, but you'll have to watch for patrols while I get it.",c="Thanks, $N. It was looking a little dicey there for a second and we've probably drawn far too much attention to ourselves.\n\nThe important part is that we have the ore sample, though, and we should get it to Ziz as soon as possible."},
[1092]={t="Gerenzo's Orders",o="Deliver the Unidentified Ore to Ziz Fizziks in the Stonetalon Mountains.",d="I guess I'd better think about getting out of here, also. It won't take long for word of what happened here to spread to the higher ups, and I'm sure they wouldn't take too kindly to meeting me again.\n\nI'll sneak out and meet with Ziz. Hopefully, he'll be able to find me a new job!\n\nI'll try and clean up this mess a little, but you should take the ore sample to Ziz right away. He told me that he'd set up camp somewhere on the western side of Windshear Crag. Good luck.",p="Something I can help you with?",c="Ahhh, I knew that I did the right thing by telling Piznik to stay behind. I'm sure the engineers in Undermine will be most interested to look at this...\n\nOf course I'll want to keep a little piece for myself, but what they don't know won't hurt them, yes?"},
[1093]={t="Super Reaper 6000",o="Get the Super Reaper 6000 Blueprints for Ziz Fizziks in the Stonetalon Mountains.",d="Terrible what the Venture Company has done here, eh? What were they thinking? Goblin company hiring a gnome!\n\nLucky for me, Sputtervalve knows a genius when he sees one. Hired me just after I'd been kicked out!\n\nTells me they built some enormous woodcutting machine, and Sput' wants me to steal the plans for him. Unfortunately, Gerenzo--bloody gnome--wants me dead on sight... maybe you could steal the plans for me? You should be able to find them on one of their operators.",p="Did you find those plans? I'm eager to impress the new boss. Hopefully, once he's convinced of my loyalty--well, as much as he can be convinced... goblin's honor, you know?--he'll feel comfortable making use of my rather impressive genius.",c="Hey, is that what I think it is? Great!\n\nNow, let's see. Ugh... how am I supposed to understand this stuff... can't figure out the way gnomes think. Lemme tell you, I'm surprised they could build the wheel, let alone those flying machines they like so much."},
[1094]={t="Further Instructions",o="Deliver the Sealed Envelope to Sputtervalve in the Barrens.",d="This envelope has all the information I was able to snatch as they booted me out the door... Venture Company internal documents, some manuals, technical things... Oh, and of course the Super Reaper 6000 blueprints.\n\nSputtervalve has taken up residence at Ratchet in the Barrens. Shouldn't have much trouble finding him, he's a little green fellow.",p="Hello there! How can I help you?",c="Fizziks, eh? Can't say I trust him, but this information seems good enough. What I wouldn't give to have the Venture Company out of my hair.\n\nThey do come up with some good machines though... I can't deny that we've benefited from using some of the improvements they've devised."},
[1095]={t="Further Instructions",o="Bring the new orders to Ziz Fizziks in the Stonetalon Mountains.",d="The matter of this gnome that has been hired by the Venture Company has caused a bit of a stir in Undermine. The trade princes do not approve of Razdunk's consorting with this Gerenzo.\n\nRiddlevox has asked me to take care of the problem, and I'm sure he was instructed to do so by one or more of the trade princes. Of course, the Director didn't tell me that. Let's just say I have a hunch.\n\nWhatever the case, Gerenzo must be removed, and it would be a fitting test to have Fizziks take care of him.",c="Eliminate Gerenzo? Now there is a prospect that I have no objections to.\n\nGnomes are bad enough as it is, but what I learned about Gerenzo only makes it worse. Apparently, he was one of the head engineers in Gnomeregan, where he was working on their secret project--we could never infiltrate Dun Morogh well enough to find out specific details. It was a failure. Our reports say that whatever it was literally exploded in their faces."},
[1096]={t="Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle",o="Bring Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle's Mechanical Arm to Ziz Fizziks in the Stonetalon Mountains.",d="I met Gerenzo once, but let me tell you, he's not easy on the eyes. His flesh looks like it's rotting away, and he's grafted metal and gears onto his body, replaced some of his limbs with mechanical ones.\n\nNortheast of here, far above Cragpool Lake, up near the water wheel is where Gerenzo watches over the entire site. There's no way I could fight my way up there, not to mention take on Gerenzo... But you look like you might be able to make it.\n\nIf you kill him for me, I'll make it worth your while!",p="Sputtervalve will want some sort of proof that Gerenzo's dead. I think his mechanical arm will probably do.",c="Look at that thing... it'd take a gnome to come up with something like that. I can't understand why you'd cut off an arm, and replace it with that, when you could just keep both arms and add a third!\n\nGnomes, I tell you...\n\nAt least Gerenzo's out of commission. Hopefully that'll be enough proof, and Sputtervalve will assign me to one of the Tinkers' Union workshops in Gadgetzan or maybe even Undermine."},
[1130]={t="Melor Sends Word",o="Speak with Melor Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff.",d="$N, Melor Stonehoof has heard of your deeds, and has set a path before you.\n\nIf you wish to take it, then go to Thunder Bluff and speak with Melor.  You will find him on Hunter's Rise.",c="So, $N, you have come.  Now, are you prepared to journey through distant lands?\n\nIf so, young $C, then listen on..."},
[1131]={t="Steelsnap",o="Bring Steelsnap's Rib to Melor Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff.",d="At times we hunt for food.  At times we hunt for honor.  And at times we hunt to earn the Earthmother's teachings.\n\nBut the hunt I now set upon you is none of these things.  It is to slay a creature outside the Earthmother's blessing.\n\nThe hyena Steelsnap roams the Thousand Needles, south of the Barrens.  He is a tyrant, attracting other hyenas to him and spreading fear and bloodshed among more peaceful beasts.\n\nFind Steelsnap, $N.  Find him, and defeat him."},
[1195]={t="The Sacred Flame",o="Return a Filled Etched Phial to Zangen Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff.",d="The Galak centaur in the Thousand Needles are protecting an artifact from the time of the centaurs' creation.\n\nWe would like to retrieve it, but we require a phial of water from one of the night elves' moonwells.\n\nTo collect the water, you will first need to obtain one of the phials carried by the dryads near the Raynewood Retreat in the heart of Ashenvale Forest. There is a moonwell near the western bank of the Falfarren River, south of the main road, where you can fill the phial."},
[1221]={t="Blueleaf Tubers",o="Grab a Crate with Holes.\nGrab a Snufflenose Command Stick.\nGrab and read the Snufflenose Owner's Manual.\n\nIn Razorfen Kraul, use the Crate with Holes to summon a Snufflenose Gopher, and use the Command Stick on the gopher to make it search for Tubers.\n\nBring 6 Blueleaf Tubers, the Snufflenose Command Stick and the Crate with Holes to Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.",d="Blueleaf tubers are a delicacy around the world!  But they're rare, very rare.  The only place to find them is here in the Barrens, deep in the earth, in Razorfen Kraul.\n\nAnd even then, they're impossible to find unless you know just where to look!  That's why I've trained these snufflenose gophers to find them for me.  They have great noses and can smell a tuber from fifty paces away.\n\nIt won't be easy, but if you get me some tubers I'll pay you handsomely."},
[1483]={t="Ziz Fizziks",o="Speak with Ziz Fizziks in Windshear Crag.",d="The Venture Company stole many of the best goblin minds, but from time to time, we get the opportunity to steal some back.\n\nA while ago, the Venture Company outfit in the Stonetalon Mountains hired Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle--a gnome! Their other engineer, Ziz Fizziks, was so taken aback by this, he pleaded with me to find him new employment with the Tinkers' Union. I set him on a few tasks, but he might need help.\n\nMaybe you could look in on him for me? He's stationed at the western edge of Windshear Crag.",c="I thought those Venture Company higher-ups were slave drivers, but then I met Sputtervalve, the cruelest of them all!\n\nHa! Though it's better than being out of a job, I suppose... Or worse, working with that Gerenzo. If you're here to help, I've got something for you to do."},
[1486]={t="Deviate Hides",o="Nalpak in the Wailing Caverns wants 20 Deviate Hides.",d="As Naralex descended deeper into his nightmare, a strange breed of beasts arose from beneath the Barrens into the Wailing Caverns.\n\nThese deviate creatures have strange, otherworldly properties. While evil in nature, it is my opinion that some good can come from their existence here in Kalimdor. I believe their hides will be of particular use in the ways of leatherworking.\n\nIf you feel up to the task, venture into the caves below and retrieve some deviate hides.",p="I am very interested in examining the hides from the deviate creatures who have infested these caves. Have you had any luck in collecting some, $C?",c="Your efforts shall not go unnoticed in gathering these hides, $N.\n\nThank you for your dedication."},
[1487]={t="Deviate Eradication",o="Ebru in the Wailing Caverns wants you to kill 7 Deviate Ravagers, 7 Deviate Vipers, 7 Deviate Shamblers and 7 Deviate Dreadfangs.",d="Naralex had a noble goal.\n\nOur great leader aspired to enter the Emerald Dream and help regrow these harsh lands back into the lush forest it once was. But something went terribly wrong.\n\nNaralex's dream turned into a nightmare and corrupt creatures began to inhabit the caverns.\n\nWhile some Disciples of Naralex seek to awake our master, my concern is with ridding these caves of the evil beasts.\n\nBrave the caverns, $N, and eradicate the deviate spawn.",c="As a Disciple of Naralex, I commend your bravery, $N.\n\nYour aid in ridding the caverns is the first step in our long plight to see the Barrens restored.\n\nThank you and may you prosper."},
[1489]={t="Hamuul Runetotem",o="Speak with Hamuul Runetotem",d="The shells you brought me have a taint, one I have never before seen.  I am certain the water of the Oases is the cause, and I can sense the confusion they cause this land.  It is as if the land dreams and cannot awake.\n\nThe Wailing Caverns must be the source of the taint.  But before you go there, speak with Hamuul Runetotem, the elder druid.  I sent word to him of the happenings in the Barrens.  He is wise, and can offer you counsel.\n\nYou will find him in Thunder Bluff, on the Elder Rise.",c="I bid you greetings, $N.  You are welcome here, and I suggest you gather all your strength.  For the task we now set before you ... is a dire one."},
[1490]={t="Nara Wildmane",o="Speak with Nara Wildmane.",d="I entered the land of dreams, and dreamed of a cult of druids who dwell in the Wailing Caverns.  I saw that their goals were once noble, but they have lost their way.  They are now servants of the taint seeping through the Barrens.\n\nI am old and my strength fails.  I could not long dwell in that dreaming place and know little more of the tainted druids.  But Nara is young and her spirit is fierce.  She remained in the dreaming when I fled.\n\nSpeak with Nara.  She is in the tent, over yonder.",c="Yes, it is true.  I know of the druids in the Wailing Caverns.  I have seen their twisted, scaled faces.  I know their crimes, and I know their plans.\n\nYou must stop them, $N."},
[1491]={t="Smart Drinks",o="Bring 6 portions of Wailing Essence to Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.",d="Ok, so the raptor horns didn't work so well.  But that's all right -- no one got rich on their first try!  And besides, I think I found something that'll work even better in my smart drinks!\n\nThere is a substance called Wailing Essence, and I think it is the cause of the strange plants and animals in the Barrens.  Get me some and I'll try it in my drink!\n\nI heard the essence gathers in ectoplasmic creatures in the Wailing Caverns to the west.  Hunt those creatures and gather the essence.",p="Where is my wailing essence?",c="Great, you got it!  I can't wait to try it out.  This is going to make me a fortune, I just know it!\n\nThank you, $N.  Take this, and after I'm rich I'll send you more, I promise!"},
[1492]={t="Wharfmaster Dizzywig",o="Bring the Secure Crate to Wharfmaster Dizzywig in Ratchet.",d="I have need to send a crate of potions, reagents and other items to my associates in the Old World. Little time I have to actually see them to the dock at Ratchet, and the last caravan has already left.\n\nIf you could, please take this to Wharfmaster Dizzywig. He will ensure that it is placed on the next boat to Blackwater Cove.",p="You seek passage on the next ship, or have some item you wish to send aboard it?",c="A small enough crate. Yes, I should be able to find room for this aboard the ship. It sails with the next tide, I trust this is soon enough? Excellent. Let me just enter it into my ledger.\n\nAll taken care of! Good day to you, $C."},
[1529]={t="Call of Water",o="Find Islen Waterseer in the Barrens.",d="Long has it been since you were last tested, $N. You have shown patience thus far in your studies, but the time has come for you to learn more. The time has come for you to learn about the purity of water.\n\nSeek out Islen Waterseer in the Barrens. She is along the eastern coast, south of the Southfury River and Ratchet. You will find her there at her fishing hut. Good luck to you, $N.",c="The wind approaches you quickly from the horizon; the earth is steady beneath your feet; and your spirit is already warmed by fire--I would say it is time for you to learn about the purity of water.\n\nYour path has led you this far, and your spirit will give you the strength to carry on even further. But the first step is yours to take."},
[1530]={t="Call of Water",o="Find Brine in Southern Barrens.",d="If there is one lesson you must learn of water, it is this: water means rebirth.\n\nIts power flows, erodes, and makes clean all manner of things. You will find its ability to heal and replenish incomparable, but only when it is pure.\n\nWhen you understand that water, when polluted, can devastate all that it touches, you will appreciate how vital a resource it is.\n\nIf you wish the water sapta, find Brine deep in Southern Barrens. Her home is continually molested by the quilboar there.",c="Yes?\n\nMmm, I have a feeling I know what you're going to ask me: what would possess someone to live out here in the deepest part of the Barrens, the threat of quilboar all around, and no protection? Well, we all have our reasons to justify why we act the way we do. The real question is, what brings a lowly skyborne to the deepest reaches of the Barrens to speak to a woman who obviously has no concern for her own well-being?\n\nI'm willing to bet we both know the answer to that."},
[1534]={t="Call of Water",o="Fill the Empty Blue Waterskin at the Ruins of Stardust in Ashenvale and return to Brine in the Barrens.",d="Take this waterskin and head deep into the lush forest the night elves call Ashenvale. It is to the far north of the Barrens.\n\nOnce you've entered the forest, travel west. Along the mountains that separate Stonetalon and Ashenvale, and beyond Lake Mystral, you will find a holy place: the Ruins of Stardust. At the center of the lake you will find a small fountain.\n\nBring me a sample of the fountain's water. It will be the final component you'll need before I send you back to Islen.",p="Do you have the water yet, $N? Tales say the ruins were protected by large creatures of nature that do not care for visitors, but those could be myths to scare off the enemies of the night elves.\n\nRegardless, be careful.",c="Wonderful, $N. With all three samples gathered, I can create for you a vial of the purest water any living creature will find. It will be used in the next steps of your rite of passage.\n\nI am pleased to count you among our kind, $N. You do all shaman proud, and I look forward to hearing about your exploits in the future."},
[1535]={t="Call of Water",o="Fill the Empty Brown Waterskin at the watering hole below Brine's hut and return it to her in the Barrens.",d="To find understanding and gain the sapta from me, you must seek out only the purest forms of water. As you fetch the samples for me, take note of your surroundings. Be aware of the creatures that rely on the water, that protect it. See how it affects forests and deserts. Witness how the very substance that sustains life will force creatures to take lives.\n\nWe shall start with a simple task: down below my hut there is a pond of the precious liquid. Fill this skin with it and return to me.",p="I am just about prepared to send you on your other tasks. Have you filled the skin yet?\n\nI know how protective the quilboar can be. Even such a small water source is a vast hoard of wealth to them. They have great feasts when even the slightest rain comes to the Barrens. Water is sacred to their kind because it is so scarce. Do you understand?",c="I thought some bloodshed might ensue if you tried to take water from the pool. It is a pity the quilboar do not realize that all living things are tied together; that their greed only perpetuates the pain and suffering of their people. How much could they accomplish if they were to put their differences aside and their clans came together.\n\nAgain, a pity, but more than likely a boon for the other races of the Barrens."},
[1536]={t="Call of Water",o="Fill the Empty Red Waterskin at the well in Tarren Mill and return to Brine in the Barrens.",d="Long ago I followed some companions into the Hillsbrad Foothills. We defended ourselves from some tenacious humans who make their home there and we found ourselves in a small town the Forsaken had taken over: Tarren Mill.\n\nIt was there I found a most peculiar thing: in the center of town was a small well of fresh spring water. I'm not sure the plagued citizens of the town even realize its value--it's a small holy vestige in an unhallowed sea.\n\nBring me a sample of that water in this waterskin.",p="The well remaining pure within the town reminds me of stories told to me when I was younger, $N. Even in times of great pain and sorrow one can find a sliver of hope, a small symbol to rally around. The orc people see Thrall this way. He survived against great odds and rose up to lead our people through his strength and example.\n\nI'm not sure any orc has suffered as much as he has, but at the same time, I'm not sure any orc is as strong as he is either.",c="This is good, $N. You're dedicated to the task at hand and have the ability to seek out that which is needed.\n\nOne more sample is all I need to create the reagent needed for your sapta. Islen will be pleased as well."},
[3261]={t="Jorn Skyseer",o="Speak with Jorn Skyseer at Camp Taurajo.",d="Your time with me is over, $N.  To learn more, you must go to Camp Taurajo to the south and speak with Jorn Skyseer.  He will continue your guidance.",c="Greetings, young one.  You are here to walk the hunter's path?\n\nVery good.  Let us begin."},
[3281]={t="Stolen Silver",o="Bring the Stolen Silver to Gazrog in the Crossroads.",d="You may have killed the raptors, but the silver they stole must be recovered!  I have reports that the raptors have a large grouping of nests south of Ratchet, known as the Raptor Grounds.  It is likely that they brought our stolen silver there.\n\nGo to this raptor haven and search for the stolen silver.  When you find it, return it to me.",p="Do you have the silver?",c="Aha!  So the raptors did hide the silver at their lair.  It's hard to believe these beasts would have the desire for silver.  Perhaps the stories of their intelligence are not as far from the mark as I thought!\n\nThank you, $N.  Take this as a reward for your service to us, and know that the guards of the crossroads owe their next month's pay to you."},
[3301]={t="Mura Runetotem",o="Speak with Mura Runetotem in the Sepulcher.",d="My clanmate, Mura Runetotem, traveled to Silverpine so that she might aid our undead allies.  Silverpine is an ailing forest, a dying forest, and it was Mura's hope to bring it new life.  Perhaps the strange life found here in the Barrens can help her work in Silverpine.\n\nTake a sample of the shells you gathered, and bring it to Mura in Silverpine.  She is staying at the Sepulcher.  With luck, studying the shell will give her the insight she needs to heal that dying place.",p="I can smell the dust of the Barrens on you, $C.  You have traveled far.",c="Ah, what is this?  This shell has an inner glow, as if it still pulses with life.  Amazing!  I must study it further.\n\nThank you, $N.  With luck, this shell will hold a secret I can use to aid the poor land of Silverpine."},
[3369]={t="In Nightmares",o="Bring the Nightmare Shard to Hamuul Runetotem on Elder Rise.",d="This shard holds great secrets; it is the pure essence of the Emerald Dream. However, what I see in this shard is not a dream; one would call this sort of a vision a nightmare.\n\nI do not wish to alarm you, $N, but I think it is best if you deliver this shard into the hands of a wise druid as soon as you can.\n\nHamuul Runetotem on Elder Rise is who you need to find. Head to Thunder Bluff. I cannot say more.",p="May I help you with something?",c="Falla sent you to me? Well now, let's see that shard that you say she was so hesitant to talk about...\n\n<Hamuul peers into the shard>\n\nOh... I didn't... Well.\n\n$N, thank you for delivering this to me. It isn't wise to speak of things such as this, though, I advise you. These are matters that you should not concern yourself with.\n\nLet's just say that things in the Emerald Dream are not as we thought...\n\nPerhaps in the future, our paths may cross again."},
[3921]={t="Wenikee Boltbucket",o="Bring the Broken Samophlange to Wenikee Boltbucket.",d="I think I might have broken that Samophlange.  That's not good, because I already told some colleagues in Undermine about it and they were very intrigued.  We must find a way to fix it!\n\nTake the broken samophlange to Wenikee Boltbucket, just south of Mor'shan Rampart, the horde outpost between the Barrens and Ashenvale.  She is very clever and inquisitive.  If you show her the samophlange I bet she'd jump at the chance to fix it.",p="I'm very busy with my work, $C.  Unless you have something for me, it'd be best if you moved along...",c="Oh, what's this?  A samophlange, you say?  What's a samophlange??\n\nAh... but look at the way it moves when you handle it.  And there's the sound of intricate gears inside.  Oh my!  I want to fix it and see what it does, don't you??"},
[3922]={t="Nugget Slugs",o="Bring 15 Nugget Slugs to Wenikee Boltbucket in the Barrens.",d="I want to fix this samophlange, but to do that I'm going to need some supplies.  I ran out of seventeen-point-five gauge nugget slugs and I'm going to need a bunch of those for the work ahead.\n\nThe closest place to get them is the Sludge Fen to the east.  The Venture Company usually keeps them in their tool buckets.  Go to the Sludge Fen and look in the tool buckets you find there, then return to me when you've gathered enough nugget slugs.",p="Do you have the nugget slugs, $N?  I've been eyeing this Samophlange and I can't wait to tinker with it.",c="Great, you got them!  Now I can get to work..."},
[3923]={t="Rilli Greasygob",o="Bring the Broken and Battered Samophlange to Rilli Greasygob in Orgrimmar.",d="Well, that didn't work.  I put some extra gauges on the samophlange to measure its structural integrity, and they read the integrity at an all-time low.  I could add some more dials and maybe a lever or two to try and fix it, but... I think that might make things even worse.\n\nYou should take the samophlange to Rilli Greasygob.  He used to work for the Venture Company -- if anyone knows how to fix it, it's Rilli.\n\nYou can find him at Nogg's Machine Shop in Orgrimmar, in the Valley of Honor.",p="Mind your head!  I don't want it to get in the way of my work!",c="What's this?  Why, it's a samophlange!  Where did you get this thing?  Have you been poking around the Venture Company holdings in the Barrens?\n\nYou must be very brave, or very stupid."},
[3924]={t="Samophlange Manual",o="Bring the Samophlange Manual to Rilli Greasygob in Orgrimmar.",d="I think I can fix the samophlange, but I'm going to need the user's manual first.  When I was in the Venture Company I had a rival, Boss Copperplug, who hoarded the secrets of the samophlange, giving out small bits of knowledge on the device to those he trusted.  I wasn't one of the trusted few...\n\nBoss Copperplug used to stay at the Boulder Lode Mine in northeastern Barrens.  Get the manual from him, and if he's given pages from it to anyone, you'll have to collect them too.",p="Do you have the manual?",c="You got the manual!  I can't wait to read it and find out how to fix the Samophlange!  I spoke with Sputtervalve in Ratchet--he wanted to thank you for your help, and wanted to reward your efforts.\n\nI want to thank you too, and if I ever get this thing fixed I'll let you know..."},
[4921]={t="Lost in Battle",o="Find Mankrik's wife and then return to him in the Crossroads.",d="We battled in a small tauren camp when we were separated--she held three of the Bristlebacks off by herself. But the odds began to overwhelm us. I led some away only to see her overwhelmed by newcomers. In my rage, I turned to face my enemies, but they brought me down easily with their vast numbers.\n\nI awoke to a tauren druid tending my wounds--he had come across me on the Gold Road as I fell.\n\nPlease, $C, find some sign of my wife."},
[5041]={t="Supplies for the Crossroads",o="Find and return Crossroads' Supply Crates to Thork in the Barrens.",d="That attack on the caravan contained supplies we desperately needed.\n\nYou've been brave enough to take on the Razormane tribe so far, and I will ask you to do so again, but this time, I wonder if I could ask you to keep your eyes open for some of our lost supplies. You can probably find them throughout their camps, the quilboar getting fat off their dishonorable acts.\n\nThe people of the Crossroads would be in your debt.",p="How goes your search for the supplies, $N? I trust the quilboar fall under your strength easily.",c="Haha! Thank you, $N! This will help us greatly. You're a boon to the Crossroads and to the Horde. If there is anything I can do for you, please, let me know."},
[5722]={t="Searching for the Lost Satchel",o="Search Ragefire Chasm for Maur Grimtotem's corpse and search it for any items of interest.",d="The troggs are not the only thing that interested Magatha in Ragefire Chasm. She has heard word that one of her servants, a Maur Grimtotem, found something peculiar while in the Chasm, but he never made it out to show her what. She'd like Maur's body found--if it still exists--and any signs of what he found while attempting to speak to the troggs.\n\nReturn to Magatha any items of interest, and I'm sure she would be very generous in her reward.\n\nAgain, seek the Chasm in the darkest areas of Orgrimmar.",c="The body looks seriously beaten by clubs or fists, but most of the corpse's clothing and equipment still looks present. It seems the troggs do not overly care much for material wealth.\n\nYou begin to search the body for anything of interest that might help Magatha."},
[5723]={t="Testing an Enemy's Strength",o="Search Orgrimmar for Ragefire Chasm, then kill 8 Ragefire Troggs and 8 Ragefire Shaman before returning to Rahauro in Thunder Bluff.",d="Beneath the city of Orgrimmar, stout creatures known as troggs started coming to the surface from deep below the lava filled tunnels. In her ever-benevolence, Magatha sought to make peace with the creatures, but they turned on her diplomats, killing them. She will not allow such treatment of the tauren people and now consider the creatures a threat to all of the Horde.\n\nShe asks that you put an end to this trogg threat before it overwhelms the Horde from below. Find Ragefire Chasm and destroy them all.",c="I am glad to see you took Magatha's task seriously. Thank you, $N. I'm sure the troggs will have a harder time coming to the surface with their numbers so greatly reduced.\n\nPerhaps in the future we can take time to figure out where such creatures came from, and what they really want."},
[5724]={t="Returning the Lost Satchel",o="Take the Grimtotem Satchel to Rahauro in Thunder Bluff.",d="You find a satchel under the body of the tauren. It is still gripped tightly in his arms as though he was trying to protect it while being attacked by the troggs.\n\nRemoving the satchel from his vice-like grip, you stow it with your own equipment and prepare to make your way out of the tunnels and back to Rahauro in Thunder Bluff.",p="Were you able to find anything, $N? Any clues as to why one of her clansman had to die needlessly would be helpful.",c="Excellent, $N. Thank you.\n\nMagatha told me that if you were successful in finding her clansman that you be given this. Please, take it in thanks."},
[5725]={t="The Power to Destroy...",o="Bring the books Spells of Shadow and Incantations from the Nether to Varimathras in Undercity.",d="Many denizens of the Legion bestow gifts on their followers as you may well know. Some of these gifts the Dark Lady feels would be better off in her hands than in the hands of those with... lesser vision.\n\nA sect of the Shadow Council hidden in caverns below Orgrimmar known as the Searing Blade are a prime example. The Lady tells me that members of the Searing Blade have come into the possession of two powerful spell books--she would like to \"borrow\" these books from them. You will get them for her.",p="There are a hundred other tasks awaiting my attention, $C. Do you have the books?",c="Good, $C. You have done well in serving the Dark Lady. Your continued perseverance and ambition will be of great use to the Lady's subjects. Return to me again in the future. Perhaps I will have other tasks for you that will aid the Dark Lady in her attempts at overtaking the Lich King and completely freeing the Scourge."},
[5726]={t="Hidden Enemies",o="Bring a Lieutenant's Insignia to Thrall in Orgrimmar.",d="One thing I will not tolerate are traitors in our midst, $N. But I would be a fool to play my hand so early--it would not sufficiently cut the corruption out of our lands and only cause the infection to grow worse.\n\nBut you, a young adventurer, could go places my agents could not... could learn the truth... could find the true head of the beast.\n\nIf you are brave enough, then enter Skull Rock to the east of Orgrimmar, find a lieutenant's insignia off one of the Burning Blade there, and return to me.",p="Do you have the insignia yet, $N?\n\nIt will be a vital tool in infiltrating what I believe is the greatest threat to the Horde, and finally finding peace in our new home.\n\nYou will learn how intricate a web men and orcs alike can weave when they are motivated by greed and power. The hidden agendas, the corruption, all of it will become clear. You will find yourself in the midst of a war you never knew existed.",c="Good, $N! The spirits be praised, perhaps you are the one who will finally put my greatest fears to rest! Who would suspect someone so young and so brave would rise up and champion our cause? You remind me of myself when I was younger. I will ensure that you are justly rewarded for your efforts if we both survive the coming storm.\n\nBut there is time for more praise later. You've not accomplished anything in comparison to what you will face... but this is a good start."},
[5727]={t="Hidden Enemies",o="Take the Lieutenant's Insignia to Neeru Fireblade and speak to him. Gauge if he believes you are a member of the Burning Blade and then return to Thrall in Orgrimmar.",d="Now let us see if this insignia you found is worth the effort.\n\nThere is a warlock within the city who believes he has my trust. He does not know that I realize where his true loyalties lie. He is in fact the leader of the Burning Blade. But do not rush off to do battle with him; he has a purpose, and we shall use him against our enemies.\n\nTake this insignia to him in the Cleft of Shadow here in Orgrimmar, speak to him and see if he believes you are one of his own, then return to me here.",c="Excellent! Most excellent, $C!\n\nWhat you have done this day is only the first step in a much broader foundation--a foundation that we will build the destruction of the Shadow Council on, once and for all.\n\nTell me all he said... and leave not one word out--it may be more important than you realize."},
[5728]={t="Hidden Enemies",o="Kill Bazzalan and Jergosh the Invoker before returning to Thrall in Orgrimmar.",d="Hmm, leaders of the Searing Blade... this concerns me most. If they are the ones of value to Neeru, then those are who we must target first. This satyr... Bazzalan, and the other Neeru mentioned--what was he, a warlock?--must be slain.\n\nReturn to the Cleft of Shadow and enter Ragefire Chasm, $N. Find these two leaders of the Searing Blade, and kill them. But be careful not to let Neeru know it was you who did this. You must retain your identity as one of his $gbrothers:sisters; in arms.",c="I am glad you've returned, $N. Some of those loyal to me brought word immediately that the caverns below Orgrimmar were in disarray now that their leaders have been slain. I even heard reports that Neeru was more than agitated. It seems we've put a dent in his armor. I can't say I'm displeased... even with such a minor victory."},
[5729]={t="Hidden Enemies",o="Speak to Neeru Fireblade in Orgrimmar.",d="I think our next step should be to have you placed close to Neeru. If he is as agitated as reports suggest, then we may accomplish two things. One, you may be able to gain some greater knowledge about the Council or at least the Burning Blade, and two, he may just begin to trust you enough that he asks you to start to aid him. He may very well look at you as someone who can fill the void now that some of the leadership is in turmoil.\n\nReturn to the Cleft and speak to him again, but do not be too overt.",c="What is it?! Oh, you, $C... my apologies. My anger rivals that of a rabid kodo bull... but perhaps it is my own fault. In sending travelers into Ragefire Chasm, I should have seen the possibility that some harm would come from it. It seems both Bazzalan and Jergosh were taken unaware and slain by some of Thrall's do-gooders. A most inopportune time, but there is nothing that can be done about it now."},
[5730]={t="Hidden Enemies",o="Speak to Thrall in Orgrimmar and tell him what you've learned.",d="You are one of my lieutenants! Prepare yourself, $C. I will call upon you soon.\n\nMy time spent on the Searing Blade may be all but wasted now, but that does not mean that the Shadow Council's schemes elsewhere must suffer. I will do what I can to minimize the damage here in Ragefire Chasm. In the meantime, I will have my agents in the Barrens and Ashenvale begin work on our newest agenda. Return to me soon.",c="Ashenvale? Hmm, I had not heard of any presence of the Council or the Burning Blade in Ashenvale. My spies will investigate, $N. You have done well.\n\nFor now, rest, and keep yourself occupied with other tasks. I will call upon you again soon.\n\nLok-Tar Ogar!"},
[5761]={t="Slaying the Beast",o="Enter Ragefire Chasm and slay Taragaman the Hungerer, then bring his heart back to Neeru Fireblade in Orgrimmar.",d="The primary task set upon me by our great Warchief is to root out the creatures responsible for infesting our lord's great city with demonic influence. The Burning Blade is one threat, but there are others; the Searing Blade for instance, who make their home in Ragefire Chasm, secretly attempting to subvert innocent members of the Horde.\n\nIf they are to be stopped, then their leader must be slain--a Felguard named Taragaman the Hungerer.\n\nKill him, and his heart will appease Thrall, of this I'm sure.",p="Have you killed the beast? He surely must be the leader of the Searing Blade in Ragefire Chasm.",c="Ha! You've done it! Thrall will be so pleased.\n\nI will ensure this heart is taken care of properly.\n\nFor now though, you must celebrate your victory. I will inform Thrall of your success.\n\nThank you for your aid, $C."},
[5881]={t="Calling in the Reserves",o="Maggran wishes you to deliver a letter to Grish Longrunner at the Great Lift in the Barrens.",d="The Horde does well keeping our troops fresh... since the Great War we have been prosperous here in Kalimdor.\n\nI need you to do me a favor, I have a lad by the name of Grish Longrunner protecting the Great Lift in the southern barrens. Give him this letter; the letter will let him know that I have a reserve warrior coming to relieve him of duty so that he can visit his family. He requested this sometime ago and he would be happy to hear the news."},
[6282]={t="Harpies Threaten",o="Maggran Earthbinder in Sun Rock Retreat wants you to slay 7 Bloodfury Harpies, 7 Bloodfury Ambushers, 7 Bloodfury Slayers and 7 Bloodfury Roguefeathers.",d="Tauren take pride as the protectors of these lands. Undoubtedly you can guess why I am alarmed with the number of harpies that dwell here in Stonetalon.\n\nThe Bloodfuries are the source of the increasing number of harpies in Kalimdor; they encroach upon all likes of life preventing the innocent from leaving their boundaries.\n\nI need you to cull the harpies, $N!"},
[6284]={t="Arachnophobia",o="Kill Besseleth and bring Besseleth's Fang to Maggran at Sun Rock Retreat.",d="Warning: Proceed into Sishir Canyon west of here at your own risk.\n\nBesseleth and her eight-legged children of the forest have claimed this canyon as their webbed lair.\n\nMaggran Earthbinder in Sun Rock Retreat has placed a bounty on Besseleth. Slay her and bring proof of your killing to Maggran; there you will receive your reward for disposing this eight-legged menace.",p="Besseleth is a ruthless predator... I fear for those that travel Webwinder Path at night. It's then that she and her children prey upon innocent travelers. I myself fell prey to her two-foot fang of death, but luckily I was able to fend her off and get to safety. I would give anything to see that monster destroyed.",c="Good hunting, $N! Besseleth is an old predator in these parts... I will miss her not. Take this reward as a token for being the forest champion.\n\n<Maggran rubs the wound caused by Besseleth.>\n\nPerhaps now many more will travel to Sun Rock Retreat without fearing what lurks in the dark."},
[6301]={t="Cycle of Rebirth",o="Tammra Windfield at Sun Rock Retreat wants you to gather 10 Gaea Seeds.",d="Industrial greed and continuous war have wrecked the lands of Stonetalon. Only the blessings of the Earthmother can cure such injury.\n\n$N, I will require you to seek a special seed, the Gaea seed. They are only found here in Stonetalon Mountain, north of Sun Rock Retreat at Mirkfallon Lake, near the water's edge.\n\nOnce you bring me the seeds I will imbue them with shamanistic power to speed their growth."},
[6393]={t="Elemental War",o="Bring 10 Incendrites to Tsunaman at Sun Rock Retreat.",d="The Tribunal of the Tides has sent me to wage war on the fire elementals here in Stonetalon Mountain. Neptulon the Tidehunter, Lord of all water elementals, has taken a personal interest in seeing our fiery cousins extinguished.\n\n$N, you can help me gain favor with the Tribunal by destroying the fire elementals in Charred Vale. When destroyed, the fire elementals leave Incendrites. Return these to me and be rewarded."},
[6421]={t="Boulderslide Ravine",o="Explore deep into the cave at Boulderslide Ravine and bring back 10 Resonite Crystals for Mor'rogal at Sun Rock Retreat to investigate.",d="Something is amiss here in Stonetalon. Can you feel the tension in the air, $N?\n\nSoutheast of here lies a deep cave in Boulderslide Ravine. The kobolds there are frantically mining a rare crystal called Resonite. I need you to bring back some ore samples so that I can understand what's happening in that cave.  I also need you to investigate the depth of that cave.\n\nGo young $c, it's imperative I know what evil lurks under these mountains.",p="What news have you discovered from Boulderslide Ravine? I recall some legend that deals with Resonite... I just cannot place my hoof on it. Perhaps knowing what lies at the bottom of the cave will illuminate their devious intentions.",c="Ah... Yes! That's it; the Resonite crystals have a trace of Earthen magic. The kobolds must have dug deep uncovering an Earthen.\n\nLegend states that the Earthen are creatures created by the Titans.  They were used to create the land our feet walk on. This most definitely is a threat that cannot be ignored.\n\n<Mor'rogal shakes his head.>\n\nPerhaps I can enchant these ore samples to use against this kobold plot."},
[6461]={t="Blood Feeders",o="Xen'zilla at Malaka'Jin needs you to kill 10 Deepmoss Creepers and 7 Deepmoss Venomspitters.",d="We Trolls here at Malaka'Jin have prospered from the land; Stonetalon Mountain offers great hunting for us to live on.\n\nLately, we have attracted the wrong dinner guests... the spiders in these mountains have been raiding our camps at night looking to steal our hunt.\n\nIf you were to help us kill off these ghastly beasts we at Malaka'Jin would be in your debt. Spiders are everywhere in Stonetalon - just head north from here and you will see what I am talking about.",c="Sweet, mon! Good news, perhaps we will have fewer unwanted dinner guests tonight.\n\nMany thanks, $N.  We are forever in your debt."},
[6481]={t="Earthen Arise",o="Open the Resonite cask with the Enchanted Resonite Crystal, and then slay Goggeroc. Return to Mor'rogal with the news and Enchanted Resonite Crystal.",d="You have uncovered a dark threat to the land, $C. The Resonite cask you have found in that cave houses a slumbering Earthen by the name of Goggeroc.\n\nI have changed the mixture of the Resonite crystals that you gathered with my shamanistic powers. Take the enchanted Resonite crystal and smash open the Resonite cask, which houses the Earthen.\n\nWhen awakened, Goggeroc will be weakened... Slay him, $N!",p="I fear if we do not dispose of this threat immediately, all of Stonetalon will be lost. The might of an Earthen can not be matched by any means. When awakened, Goggeroc will be weak from his long slumber, this will be the opportunity that you must take advantage of... go now $N!",c="You bear good news, $C! I fear the possibilities of what an Earthen would mean to Kalimdor.\n\nSlaying Goggeroc was a task for no one less than a hero. You have done well; all of Stonetalon and Kalimdor are indebted to you, noble $C.\n\nAccept this as your reward most honored one."},
[6541]={t="Report to Kadrak",o="Report to Kadrak at the watch tower in northern Barrens.",d="Have you ever been to Ashenvale, to the north? The horde has recently set up an outpost on the Zoram Strand there, and we can always use some new recruits to help defend our new fronts.\n\nIf you think you are up to it, see Kadrak in the northern Barrens, at the watch tower. He is heading up the Ashenvale campaign and can give you further orders."},
[6542]={t="Report to Kadrak",o="Report to Kadrak at the watch tower in northern Barrens.",d="Have you ever been to Ashenvale, to the north? The horde has recently set up an outpost on the Zoram Strand there, and we can always use some new recruits to help defend our new fronts.\n\nIf you think you are up to it, see Kadrak in the northern Barrens, at the watch tower. He is heading up the Ashenvale campaign and can give you further orders."},
[6548]={t="Avenge My Village",o="Kill 8 Grimtotem Ruffians and 6 Grimtotem Mercenaries, and then return to Makaba Flathoof near the southeastern edge of Stonetalon.",d="The Grimtotem Clan raided my village and killed most everyone. I killed all I could, but barely escaped with my life.\n\n$N, all I wish now is that more of them are dead. You will find them just to the west of here.",c="$N, I thank you... but I will never forget what the Grimtotem have done to my village."},
[6562]={t="Trouble in the Deeps",o="Speak to Je'neu Sancrea in Ashenvale.",d="Je'neu Sancrea is in need of aid. He is at the Zoram'gar Outpost in Ashenvale. The Night elf forest is to the north of the Stonetalon mountains. You can reach it by traveling through Windshear Crag or by heading north through Barrens. Zoram Strand is far to the west of the forest. Be careful, $N. There are forces there that will not take to your presence kindly."},
[6629]={t="Kill Grundig Darkcloud",o="Kill Grundig Darkcloud and 6 Grimtotem Brutes, and return to Makaba Flathoof near the southeastern edge of Stonetalon.",d="$N, you've done a fine job killing Grimtotem. If you dare, Grundig Darkcloud and his personal band of brutes is by far the worst of the lot. He was the one who led the brutal attack on my village.\n\nYou will find him in Grimtotem Post a bit further up the path to the west. Kill him, and I will be forever grateful.",c="Grundig Darkcloud is dead! $N, I will always be grateful for what you've done here today."},
[6981]={t="The Glowing Shard",o="Travel to Ratchet to find someone that can tell you more about the glowing shard.\n\nThen, deliver the shard as you are directed.",d="The shard is a brilliant green, and although solid, what looks like smoke swirls just below the surface. You can't help staring into the depths of the crystal; at the same time, you know there is something very disturbing about it.\n\nMaybe you should see if anyone in Ratchet can tell you more about this strange shard.",p="Hello, skyborne. What can I do for you?",c="Oh... I have never seen anything like this..."},
[79007]={t="... and that note you found",o="Charred remains of the note serve as your only guide.",d="<The faint radiance of the embers darkening, you stumble across the remnants of a recent fire.\n\nAmidst the scattered provisions, you discover a blistered note.>\n\n\"Not all that burns is lost. Find the twin land, find the place.\""},
[86576]={t="Bloodfury Trinkets",o="Bring 15 Glittering Sunstones to Mor'rogal.",d="In addition to spreading their filth across the Charred Vale, the Bloodfury harpies gather anything shiny that they can find. I'm told that they collect a variety of golden-yellow sunstones for decoration. I have no use for such trinkets, but Mor'rogal has mentioned using them before.\n\nWhile you're fighting the harpies of the Vale, keep your eye out for Glittering Sunstones. Bring any that you find to Mor'rogal, up on the hills above us."},
[92401]={t="A Frightened Request",o="Investigate the disappearance of Edward Heartweaver in the Ruins of Lordaeron.",d="It's my husband Edward...\n\nHe has not returned from his weekly journey to the graveyard in the Lordaeron ruins. Our son was lost when Arthas razed the city, and my dear Edward is still filled with guilt and sorrow that we never found his body. I've tried to warn him against searching those overrun ruins, but he refuses to give up. I try not to worry, but it's been days.\n\nThere are things there I cannot contend with but if you are willing, I need to know the fate of my husband.",c="What I asked of you was not fair, nor would it have been unjust for you to simply walk away. Thank you stranger. I am unable to repay you in kind but I hope one of these is acceptable.\n\nI hope our paths cross again without such sorrow."},
[92421]={t="Light's Justice",o="Collect 25 Intact Limbs within The Ruins of Lordaeron for Morbin Lightbane in the Undercity.",d="As a paladin of the Forsaken, it is my duty to exact the will of our Dark Lady while tending to our people's needs. We are fortunate with an opportunity to accomplish both.\n\nAbove the Undercity, the scourge still roam unchecked in great numbers. Our forces dwindle trying to reclaim our land, and decaying flesh cannot be reknit. Not without replacements.\n\nWould that our glorious captain Garek Bandarion still be with us, I know what he would wish. To finish what he started and heal our kin. For Lordaeron!",p="What remains of the invading scourge? Have you managed to find suitable replacement parts?",c="Let those who fall from the Banshee Queen's grace meet our justice!\n\nWith these parts, our brothers and sisters have hope to see another day. You do Captain Bandarion proud."},
[92422]={t="The Wrath of Rath'mael",o="Kill Rath'mael in the Ruins of Lordaeron for Deathguard Kristof in Brill.",d="Reports have come in from the Lordamere Overlook deep within the Ruins of Lordaeron. An unholy fog has taken over the streets and graveyard, affording the scourge up there some measure of stealth. \n\nOur scouts indicate they're being conjured by a new power within their ranks, a necromancer known as Rath'mael. We do not have the luxury of waiting this one out, $N.\n\nIf you have allies, summon them and their aid to the Forsaken. Drive this creature out of our lands.",c="While I have no doubt something of his kind will be replaced, we can only hope their ranks thin in the meantime.\n\nThank you $N."},
[92460]={t="Coming of Age",o="Speak with Rorian the Dayseeker in Thendal Grove.",d="Look at you, bright eyed and ready for adventure! We need all the help we can get here in Thendal Village and your arrival is most welcome. I imagine you are brimming with nerves for what is to come. After all, you only get to come of age once in a lifetime.\n\nGo, seek out our village leader Rorian the Dayseeker at the entrance to the greatfather tree just west of here. He will get you started on your journey.",c="Gale's greetings, $N. I am honored to bestow your coming of age relic today as you are recognized for the potential you bring to the shen'dorei. Our people have faced great hardship and persecution in our complex history.\n\nToday you are given this relic which is one of many held by those before you. Someday when your ashes are scattered to the winds it will pass to another to continue our tradition.\n\nAs you take this relic with you know that the winds of home will be with you wherever you travel."},
[92461]={t="Harmony in Balance",o="Slay 8 Vuldren Juveniles in Thendal Grove.",d="We live in times of great uncertainty for our people. We face unprecedented challenges that may require bold solutions, but we also must contend with the ordinary and mundane here in Thendal Grove. Take, for example, the recent unsustainable rise in the vuldren population.\n\nThe vuldren are a vital part of our ecosystem. However, imbalances must be corrected to maintain the delicate harmony that all creatures in Thendal Grove share.\n\nHead east and cull some of the vuldren there.",c="Thank you for your service to Zephras, young $C.\n\nThe vuldren are typically quite docile, but the animals that call Zephras home can sense when the magic on the winds is out of balance, which can lead to dangerous and unpredictable behavior if left unchecked."},
[92462]={t="Infestation Investigation",o="Slay 8 Pesky Cirrusflies in Thendal Grove.",d="One of our rangers recently reported an infestation of cirrusflies here in Thendal Grove. \n\nCirrusflies can be dangerous if the swarm is allowed to grow too large, so please head to the eastern end of the Grove and exterminate as many as you can.",c="Judging by the amount of bug entrails covering you, this must be quite the infestation."},
[92463]={t="The Cirrusfly Queen",o="Destroy the Cirrusfly Queen in Thendal Grove.",d="If the forest is as thick with these insects as it sounds, simply killing the workers won't be enough.\n\nGo deeper into the forest and find the queen. She'll be close to the hive and surrounded by bigger and more aggressive soldiers, so be careful.\n\nPut her down and return here when it's done. That'll be one less problem to think about around here.",c="Excellent work, $N. You'd make a fine ranger if this whole \"adventurer\" thing doesn't work out for you."},
[92464]={t="Elemental Unrest",o="Speak to Yala Windwatcher in Thendal Grove.",d="Ever since our elemental benefactors left us, it seems that we are simply moving from one unrest to another. The problem we face now is that the manifestations of the winds near the standing stones to the northeast are agitated.\n\nNot truly self-aware like the sentient wind spirits that once lived here, these simple sprites respond in kind to forces, emotions, and intentions of the creatures around them. \n\nMy apprentice Yala Windwatcher went to observe them. Seek her out and discover what she's learned.",c="Rorian sent you? Good. I could use your aid."},
[92465]={t="Agitators",o="Slay 6 Roiling Winds and 7 Al'Aketh Converts in Thendal Grove.",d="The Al'Aketh cult is a blight upon this island. These cultists are surely the ones responsible for agitating the simple wind sprites that reside here and turning them violent.\n\nRegrettably, we'll need to disperse these roiling winds here before they harm someone. We also need to send a clear message to the cult that they are not welcome in the grove.\n\nWill you lend me your aid, $C?",c="It pains me to shed shen'dorei blood here in the grove, but we do what we must."},
[92466]={t="Call of Earth",o="Bring a Signet of Akir to Windshaper Boro.",d="While we owe much of our prosperity to the elements of wind, the path we walk requires that we obey the call of all four of the primary elements and undertake a trial for each. Before you begin your first trial in earnest however, you must prove the strength of your resolve.\n\nTravel to the standing stones to the east. A force of Al'Aketh converts has been spotted there and they must be driven off. Confront the cultists there and bring me one of their signets as proof of your deeds.",p="The Al'Aketh cult represents the most direct and urgent danger to our homeland. Their increasingly extremist actions have destabilized our society and damaged our already-weakened connection to the spirits of the four winds. The elements demand action to prove our resilience and resolve, which are traits that are endemic to the domain of the element of earth.",c="You have returned and brought what I have requested and thus your grit and determination are unquestionable. You are ready for the next step, $N."},
[92467]={t="Call of Earth",o="Find the Rise of Spirits and drink the Earth Sapta.",d="A sapta is a drink created to bind our spirits to the elements. Fused with magic, the potion will allow the strong willed to see the elements as no one else can. Your spirit will be connected to the element the sapta was created for, and only a select few shaman know the recipe.\n\nThe sapta is always drunk in a sacred place, and never anywhere else--remember that.\n\nSeek out the Rise of Spirits up the pass east of here. Drink your sapta there, and... well, you will see what you need to see.",c="Ah... $N... child of the four winds... You seek understanding. You seek answers. Why have the winds left you? How may you get them back? These are answers I cannot provide, for I do not know the motives or movements of the winds.\n\nI can, however, teach you much of the earth. Its strength, its resolve. Even here, high in this endless sea of clouds, you are still a creature of the earth. If you hope to find the strength to speak to the spirits of the four winds once more, this is the path you must walk."},
[92468]={t="Call of Earth",o="Bring the Rough Quartz to Windshaper Boros in Thendal Grove.",d="Take this Rough Quartz from me and bring it to the one you call Windshaper Boro as proof of our meeting. He will craft a totem for you, and this shard will be the heart of it. As small as it may seem, you will come to find that size does not matter, and that even the smallest of things can outlast many others.\n\nBe patient, $N. Remain strong. And seek wisdom. This is what the elements ask of you. In the end, you shall become one with the earth--respect it as it shall respect you.",p="As you will come to learn, the path we walk is not as simple as it may seem. While we seek to find the voice needed to speak with the spirits of the winds, the winds are but one of the elemental forces of this world. Only through understanding, and--we hope--mastery of all four elements will we regain our voice to again sing the songs of the wind.",c="Good!\n\nThe totem I will craft for you is more than a symbol of your status among shaman--it has abilities beyond that. One use of the totem is as a focus for spells. Those spells are tied to the earth, and as you earn greater and greater wisdom, more of the earth's abilities will be made accessible to you.\n\nThe trainers will know when you are ready for greater knowledge.\n\nBut for now, take this earth totem..."},
[92469]={t="Return to Rorian",o="Bring word of the Al'Aketh to Rorian the Dayseeker in Thendal Grove.",d="You've done enough here, $C. I'll stay and clean up any stragglers down there.\n\nHead back to the Village and tell Rorian about the cult's presence. He will not be pleased.",c="This is most troubling, but unfortunately unsurprising. We've been aware of the cult's movements for some time, but we've been content to watch from afar. Their agitation of the wind spirits near the standing stones is a clear escalation on their part.\n\nYou've performed a difficult but necessary service for Thendal Grove, $N. Thank you."},
[92470]={t="Foul Matriarch",o="Slay 8 Ursera Scavengers and collect the head of the den mother, Urs'anah in Thendal Grove.",d="Rorian informed you that I've been watching you. I now offer you a test of resolve. However, be warned--it will send you into great danger.\n\nGo to the caves to the west. Thin out the ursera's numbers there, and find their matriarch, one the rangers call \"Urs'anah\". Put her down and bring me proof of her demise. Once you have done that, you will have taken an important step on your path.",p="What I ask of you is not easy, but you must be prepared for much greater challenges if you are to survive long enough to be of service to Zephras Isle.",c="Very well done. You've felled beasts and laid low cultist interlopers. You have shown great promise but your path must soon take you beyond the relative safety of Thendal Village."},
[92471]={t="Aetheen of the Gales",o="Speak with Aetheen of the Gales in Thendal Grove.",d="You may not realize this but everything you've done has been a trial of sorts. A test for what is to come for you. It's a big island out there, and Zephras needs spirited young adventurers such as yourself if we are to survive the trials our people face.\n\nThe one called Aetheen of the Gales is one of the leaders of our people here on Zephras Isle, and she has been watching you. She has a task that you must complete. Speak with her to learn more.",c="Rorian has told me much of you. I am likely unknown to you, but I am a member of the Council of Elders here on Zephras Isle. I've come to read the flow of the winds here in Thendal Grove. I'm also here to assess young shen'dorei such as yourself that are coming of age.\n\nSo tell me, are you ready to take your next step? Are you ready to serve Zephras Isle?"},
[92472]={t="The Next Step",o="Report to Constable Aonda in Shen'dar Village.",d="One of the most pervasive threats on Zephras Isle is the Al'Aketh Cult. They are religious zealots devoted to the worship of the supposed elemental ruler of Skywall, Al'Akir the Windlord. They are brutal, single-minded, and their power and ambitions are growing more deadly by the day.\n\nYour path will soon take you to Shen'dar Village to the south. Present yourself to Constable Aonda when you arrive. The cult threatens Shen'dar and they are in need of aid. Tell Aonda that I sent you.",c="Aetheen sent you, then? I'll confess, you don't look like much to me, but Shen'dar Village won't turn down willing aid, much less aid sent from Elder Aetheen herself."},
[92473]={t="Aggressive Encroachment",o="Collect 6 Scrawny Ursera Claws from Scrawny Ursera in Thendal Grove.",d="The ursera den to the southwest is rapidly becoming a problem. Just last week the rangers had to kill an adolescent ursera who wandered too close to the village and attempted to attack a boy playing near the base of the elder tree in the center of the village.\n\nWe were fortunate that the boy escaped with his life. Hunger and desperation makes these beasts too dangerous to be left unchecked. Go south and put the scrawniest among the ursera down. Bring me their claws as proof when it is done.",p="The ursera have grown far more aggressive of late. I wonder what has changed to cause this shift in behavior?",c="Well done, $C. The Rangers of the Grove are in your debt."},
[92474]={t="Falling With Style",o="Jump from the top of the watchtower in Thendal Grove and use your Walk on Air ability to slow your fall.",d="Well hello there, $N! Want to play a game?\n\nAll you've got to do is step up on that ledge... then jump! Use your innate ability to walk on the air to slow your fall and see how far forward you can float.\n\nThe rules are made up and the points don't matter, but you get bonus points if you can land right in front of Rorian the Dayseeker and startle him! He won't like it but I'll certainly get a good laugh if you can get him all worked up! Hah!",c="How many times do I need to tell Myriaal not to encourage others to make reckless usage of our skyborne gifts!\n\nThat being said, I suppose that a little bit of practice in the relative safety of the village is... acceptable.\n\nIn the future I'd simply suggest you to use your ability judiciously. You do not want to exhaust your magic thoughtlessly and then not be able to use it when you truly need it."},
[92484]={t="Embracing the Elements",o="Examine the Humming Recall Crystal then speak with Windshaper Boro in Thendal Grove.",d="While you were away dealing with our vuldren problem, our resident Shaman trainer--Windshaper Boro--left this recall crystal for you. Please examine it, then speak with Boro just over yonder near the center of the village.",p="Winds guide you, $N.",c="Can you hear it? The whispers of the winds? Doubtful, considering that the spirits stopped speaking with us when they left us those years ago. \n\nThose among us who would seek audience with the spirits of the four winds once more hone our understanding of the elements and the natural world, dearly hoping to reestablish the dialogue that was so abruptly ended. \n\nWould you walk this path and master the elements?\n\nSpeak with me again if you wish to take your next steps and I will train you."},
[92514]={t="Welcome to Shen'dar Village",o="Speak with Illaya Amberwind and Coriella Calmbreeze in Shen'dar Village.",d="You've got that \"Windshaper\" air about you. Something about how I can feel a tiny bit of static on my skin when near someone spirit-touched that gives it away. Before I properly put you to work around here, you should check in with our resident Windshaper elder, Illaya Amberwind. She's just outside, near the center of town.\n\nOh, and check in with Coriella Calmbreeze as well, she runs the local inn and can provide lodging and supplies, should you need them.",c="Checked in with Illaya then? Great. Lots of tension between the High Order and the Windshapers these days, but they keep things civil here in Shen'dar. Everyone here is well aware that we've got bigger problems than their quibbles.\n\nNow that that's done, you look like someone who might be looking for something to do with their hands and I've got a bandit problem that I was hoping you could help me with."},
[92515]={t="The Problem With Prideclaws",o="Collect 10 Prideclaw Pelts from the Prideclaws in Shen'dar Highlands.",d="As if bandits and mad cultists weren't enough, the hills are thick with prideclaws as well right now. They are starting to encroach on the village borders and growing bolder by the day. It's only a matter of time before someone's pet or child is taken. It would be a mercy for us to cull their numbers now rather than after some tragedy occurs.\n\nBring me a dozen or so of their pelts. I can turn them into all sorts of goods that will be of aid to the village.",p="If you ask me, I think Prideclaws are actually kind of cute. From a safe distance... and while standing behind someone holding a sword, of course.",c="I didn't say it wouldn't be a dirty job, did I?"},
[92516]={t="Hippogryph Harassment",o="Slay 8 Hippogryph Youths, 6 Hippogryph Protectors and a Hippogryph Matriarch in the Shen'dar Highlands.",d="A flock of Hippogryph have recently established nesting grounds southeast of Shen'dar Village and they've been wreaking havoc on travelers on the road. I need someone to head down there and thin them out for us.",c="Well done, and quickly too. Not too bad at all."},
[92517]={t="The Criminal Element",o="Kill 10 Highlands Bandits and their leader, \"Badwind\" Bennic in the Shen'dar Highlands.",d="There's a cave not far to the north, hidden behind a waterfall. It's well known to me that there's a group of bandits that are operating out of that cave. They were a problem for us before the cult arrived, but now they are a real terror. I can't spare the people to go and clear them out, unfortunately.\n\nI need you to go there and take care of them for me. Kill as many as you can, and if possible, take out their leader, the one they call \"Badwind\" Bennic. That cave is dangerous, so be careful.",c="With the bandits dispersed, that is one less problem for us to deal with. Though I confess that now I worry that any bandits who survived may turn next to the cult for protection, further bolstering their increasingly alarming numbers.\n\nStill though, we'll take the victories where we can get them."},
[92528]={t="Among the Faithful",o="Look around Falaath Village to learn about the cult's intentions in the Shen'dar Highlands.",d="The faithful of Al'Akir grow ever stronger with each eager new recruit like yourself. As you can see, our strength gives form to the storm itself!\n\nNormally I'd send you straight to Skypriest Aanders for assessment, but he is occupied at present receiving a guest at the inn on the north side of town. Please avoid that place for now. An unshaven recruit like yourself in the presence of such a guest would be inappropriate.\n\nFor now, just don't get in anyone's way.",c="Lorthuna herself was there? She's the leader of the whole damned cult!\n\nIf they are making a move on Shen'dar Village and the western watchtower, we've got to be ready. What is strange is... why the watchtower?\n\nThe Village I can understand, but the tower? It doesn't have much strategic significance, other than as a minor lookout post.\n\nRegardless, we will be prepared for them. They'll find that highlanders aren't as easy to catch flat footed as they might think."},
[92529]={t="Falaath Village",o="Report to Missionary Jasaan near the entrance to Falaath Village.\n\nIf you lose your Mark of Akir, speak with Sania Silverstream in Shen'dar Village to regain the effect.",d="It gladdens my heart that you wish to serve Al'Akir. Our current trials as a people stem from our own complacency. We grew prideful and took the bounty of the winds for granted. The stagnation that followed is the reason the spirits of the wind abandoned us.\n\nOnly through acts of contrition may we feel the wind's caress once more. If you seek the fellowship of like-minded shen'dorei, go to Falaath Village and find Missionary Jasaan there. I will mark you so that the faithful will know you as a recruit.",c="What is this? A new acolyte seeking to serve the windlord sent by sister Sania? Truly we are blessed by the touch of the four winds this day!\n\nWe welcome all who seek to bask in the blessings of Al'Akir."},
[92544]={t="Al'Aketh Thugs",o="Slay 6 Al'Aketh Brutes, 4 Al'Aketh Neophytes, and Malduko Cloudcrush in Thendal Grove.",d="A band of Al'Aketh cult ruffians have taken up residence near the temple ruins just southwest of here, led by a real monster called Malduko Cloudcrush. This rabble has no doubt been dispatched here by High Priestess Lorthuna at the Shrine of Akir to attack travelers and coerce our people into joining the cult.\n\nI need to stay here at my post to alert travelers leaving the grove of the danger, but I would be grateful if you could do something about those cultists and their leader for me.",c="It was all I could do to stop myself from going over and joining you from my position here. I can only hope that these louts got the message and clear out of here soon. \n\nThank you, $C. You have the gratitude of the Rangers of Thendal Grove."},
[92550]={t="Havoc in the Highlands",o="Travel to the ruins of Falaath Village and slay 6 Al'Aketh Stormcallers, 4 Living Lightning and take the head of Commander Cyclas.",d="Our best defense here might just be a strong offense. The advantage we now have is that we expect an attack is coming. What they won't expect is for us to hit them first.\n\nI've already asked a lot of you, but please head back over to Falaath Village. Kill as many cultists as you can and if you can get close enough, kill the commander and bring me his head. I'll stay here and organize the citizens and our few peacekeepers to prepare a defense... just in case you don't return.",p="It feels good to turn the tables on these zealots.",c="Thank the winds you've returned!\n\nSania Silverstream snuck out of town just before you returned, no doubt fleeing at the sight of our people arming themselves.\n\nYou've done an incredible thing for the people of Shen'dar Village and we owe you a debt of gratitude. If the cult returns to the highlands, they will find that Shen'dar is not such an easy target.\n\nWinds guide you, $N."},
[92551]={t="Stolen Supplies",o="Collect 10 packs of Stolen Shen'dar Supplies from Falaath Village in the Shen'dar Highlands.",d="I overheard you might be going to Falaath Village? While you are there, please keep an eye out for our stolen supply caches.\n\nThe Al'Aketh have been raiding our supply caravans carrying various goods such as food and windstones to and from the lowlands for months. They've been blaming the bandits, of course, but we all know that it all ends up in the same place. If there's any of that stuff left in Falaath, it would be a huge help if you could recover it.",p="There's a lot of hungry and desperate skyborne here who need these supplies.",c="This is great! We've been barely squeaking by without our regular supply deliveries. I'll work with the constable to ensure that these supplies get redistributed to the townsfolk who are in most dire need."},
[92553]={t="Restocking the Larders",o="Collect 3 Small Eggs and 8 Strider Meat from creatures found throughout the Shen'dar Highlands.",d="Up for a bit of work? I could use a bit of muscle from a strong adventuring-type such as yourself. With how dangerous things are getting around here, no one's had much time to hunt or forage of late, and I need someone to get out there and source me fresh eggs and strider meat to keep this village fed.\n\nI'd be happy to teach you one of my famous recipes if you can bring me what I need. What do you say?",p="No matter how much things change here on Zephras and how uncertain things get, I always say that a pipe full of dried peacebloom and nice full belly is a comfort that can't be beat!",c="These eggs aren't easy to get but wind save me, they are DELICIOUS fried up in a bit of ursera tallow.\n\nIf you've got a bit of time to spare and you enjoy cooking, I can teach you a few tips and tricks I've picked up. Say the word and I'd be happy to train you."},
[92579]={t="To Valanaar",o="Deliver Aonda's Written Report to Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar.",d="For now it seems the pylon and the village are safe, so I'd like you to deliver this report to Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar, at the southeastern edge of the island. Valennia is the leader of the peacekeepers on the island and she needs to know what happened here.\n\nThe cult is expanding rapidly and the peacekeepers have avoided direct conflict until now, but those days are over. Valanaar will need to be ready for a fight.\n\nAt any rate, thank you. You'll always have friends in Shen'dar, $N.",p="A letter from Aonda. What's that crafty highlander been up to?",c="<Valennia's expression darkens as she reads the letter.>\n\nAonda trusted you to deliver this and she speaks highly enough of you in this letter, so I'll try to trust you too. Before we speak further, I need to consult with the few peacekeepers we have left here and formulate a plan in case the cult strikes here next. Enjoy your stay in Valanaar for now.\n\nIf you are looking to keep yourself busy, there are plenty of townsfolk that can likely use the help of a strong young adventurer like yourself."},
[92595]={t="The Windshapers",o="Listen to what Illaya Amberwind has to say.",d="<Illaya smiles warmly at you.> \n\nI am glad you returned to speak with me, child of the winds. I knew it the first moment you walked into my presence, that you were strong in the skysight. Even for a Shaman, you show particular aptitude in our gift.\n\nCome, let us speak about the mandate of the Windshapers, the nature of our struggles on Zephras, and the plight of our people.",c="I think you now understand how important the mission of the Windshapers is. Every soul who commands the skysight is of vital importance if we hope to establish dialogue with the spirits of the winds once again.\n\nBetween threats from within such as the Al'Aketh, and the uncertainty of our safety here in Skywall, it is our responsibility as Windshapers to use our gifts to save our home and ensure that the Shen'dorei can survive these trying times."},
[92598]={t="The Gift of Skysight",o="Use your Skysight racial ability at the Elemental Convergence in Thendal Grove.",d="As a Windshaper, you have the ability to use the sacred skysight gifted to us by the elemental spirits. Travel to the standing stones to the northeast of the village. Find the elemental convergence there and use your gift.\n\nYou'll find that you may draw upon the skysight anywhere, but its boon is much more powerful if you do so in the presence of an elemental convergence. You may at times receive other bits of wisdom from the spirits that are drawn to such places of power, as well.",c="Like a muscle, your skysight must be exercised if you hope to grow stronger in the gift. Leveraging your skysight to bridge the distance between the mortal and the spiritual may prove invaluable to you in your adventures.\n\nYou'd do well to remember what you've learned here today. Our ability to use our gifts to hear what the elements tell us could be the key to our survival."},
[92640]={t="Desperate Times",o="Speak with Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar and follow her instructions.",d="Since engaging the cult in the open is not viable, our best chance is going to be to use this opportunity to attack the shrine itself. We can take Lorthuna herself off the board before she can finish her part of this scheme.\n\nIt so happens that Valennia has been preparing a strategy for a potential assault on the Shrine for some time now. The only problem is, we will need help. \n\nSpeak with Valennia for the details.",c="Tensions between the Windshapers and High Order are high right now, but we couldn't hope to carry out this plan without both groups on board."},
[92642]={t="Disrupting Logistics",o="Slay 4 Al'Aketh Healers and 8 Al'Aketh Brawlers in the Gustberry Lowlands.",d="Valennia only sent one person to help repel a full-scale assault... by the winds.\n\nYou don't look like much but I'll take what I can get. We need to inflict as much damage as possible to stop this soon. My people can't hold out much longer.\n\nGo down the hill and disrupt their logistics. Their healers are keeping the attackers coming, if we take them out we might be able to rally and push them back. Any other cultists you kill while you are out there are helpful as well.",c="You are still alive? Thank the winds for small miracles, I suppose."},
[92643]={t="The Turncoat",o="Find the cultist turncoat at the house just inside the highlands northwest of Valanaar.",d="There is a turncoat amongst the Al'Aketh. They claim to know the cult's true intentions for the island and want to come in, but will only do so with assurances of protection.\n\nThis defector is hiding at a secluded residence just northwest of Valanaar inside the highlands. I need someone who can discreetly go there, find the traitor, and escort him back to us. This might be a trap, but if this information is as important as this traitor claims, it's worth some risk.",c="<This man is clearly dead, killed by the assassins that you fought outside the house. As you kneel down to inspect the body you notice the glinting reflection of something shiny...>"},
[92644]={t="Unfortunate News",o="Deliver the glowing crystal to Talanaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.",d="<You reach beneath the still-warm body of the turncoat cultist and recover a small, glowing blue crystal. It appears to be damaged, but it may still be important. High Elder Shadowsong may be interested in this.>",p="You are back? And... alone?",c="The turncoat was already dead when you arrived, you say? This is unfortunate news.\n\n<You hand over the crystal you found on the dead cultist's body.>\n\nInteresting..."},
[92645]={t="Breaking the Breaker",o="Slay Commander Belguilos in the Gustberry Lowlands.",d="This attack is going to be hard to repel unless we can take out the cult commander. Belguilos \"the Breaker\" they call her, and she's a veritable terror. She used to be a peacekeeper before the cult got out of control, and even then she was... off. As a cultist I can only imagine how much worse she could be now.\n\nI might just be sending you to your death, but someone needs to take Belguilos out if we are going to survive here. You can find her at the villa at the hill's base. Good luck, $C.",c="Belguilos is dead? Four winds bless you, $C. \n\nWe might just make it out of this alive after all."},
[92646]={t="Confront Lorthuna",o="Take the portal to the Rohashi Spires overhead and join Elaadrin Evengale and Ayessa Dawnsinger in their confrontation with the High Priestess Lorthuna.",d="Lorthuna fled up to the spires above using some sort of portal. Ayessa and Elaadrin went in after her. That was just a few moments ago.\n\nI'm afraid I took one too many hits and this is where I stay. Go through the portal, find Ayessa and help them stop Lorthuna.\n\nUnless that help that Elaadrin and Ayessa said they sent for arrives soon, you are on your own from here. Good luck, $C.",c="I sent a few of our healers to ensure that Valennia and her remaining forces made it back in one piece. She should be resting in the High Elder's residence now.\n\nMuln has already departed back to Azeroth, but he and I spoke of what is next for the Windshapers and our mission to Azeroth. Unfortunately, the island is more vulnerable than ever now and we need a plan to protect Zephras from what is to come."},
[92679]={t="Blood Tithe",o="Listen to what Alvarion Windfield has to say and find Aamelia Windfield at the Windfield Orchard.",d="H--Hello, stranger. You have the look of a capable adventurer about you. I...\n\n<The Skyborne man winces, clearly suffering terrible pain>\n\n...I was wondering if you were seeking employment? I came here to Valanaar to recruit fighters to help save my farm. If you are interested, please go find my wife Aamelia Windfield at our orchard to the west of Valanaar, in the lowlands.",p="What? Alvarion is alive?",c="<Aamelia listens while you explain what became of Alvarion.>\n\nAt least I know he's going to be safe in Valanaar.\n\nStranger, I hate to tell you this but I think my idiot husband likely just sent you here to die for nothing. If you have any sense at all, you should leave now. This isn't your fight."},
[92682]={t="Make Yourself Useful",o="Gather 10 Ripe Stormapples and slay 5 Hungry Bandits at the Windfield Orchard.",d="Oh, so you've got more courage than sense, then? Fine, I won't argue.\n\nFerauu and his goons aren't due to pick up their take of the harvest just yet, so I'm going to put you to work for your meals until they arrive.\n\nHead outside and gather today's batch of stormapples for me. Oh, and the bandits lurking around the stormapple trees... They think they are sneaky. They aren't. Kill them for me. \n\nLet's see what you've got in a fight.",p="These bandits are more likely to double cross and steal from each other than they are to steal from normal folks. I bet if Ferauu knew some of his people went rogue and came here early to tamper with the harvest, he'd kill them himself.",c="I watched you take down those bandits from the window. Not bad."},
[92683]={t="Flutterfly Dust",o="Gather 5 Flutterfly Dust from the Flutterflies around the Gustberry Lowlands.",d="I'm sure you've noticed the giant flutterflies out in the outer fields near the orchard? They are pleasant to look at, but they also have other benefits; namely their wing dust. It can be a mess, but if you can gather it up in large amounts, it has useful household applications.\n\nTake this Flutterfly Swatter and give the big bugs a good swat for me. They'll usually just get scared and flee, but sometimes they'll take some offense. Either way, they'll give their rumps a shake and drop a pile of dust.",p="Flutterflies are normally docile and calm, but rub them the wrong way and sometimes they'll surprise you.",c="This stuff can be a bit messy and it tends to get everywhere. You'll probably be shaking this out of your trousers for weeks, unfortunately. I do appreciate it, though. I've had this on my to-do list for weeks, but getting too far from the house when it's just me on my own with bandits lurking everywhere is a big risk.\n\nDon't bother asking me what I use this stuff for. Things. Stuff and things. Don't worry about it."},
[92684]={t="Ornery Ornery Galestriders",o="Gather 7 Lowlands Galestrider Tenderloins from the Ornery Galestriders found throughout the Gustberry Lowlands.",d="As if the harvest wasn't light enough this year already, the galestriders in the area have been getting into the orchard and stealing my stormapples. Think you can head out to the fields and cull them for me?\n\nTake care though stranger, these lowlands galestriders are bigger and angrier than the highlands variety. Watch yourself. A well-timed kick is all it takes to put you down for good if you aren't paying attention.\n\nBring me some of their meat and I can make us a hot meal with it as well.",p="I don't think I've had real meat for dinner in... well, too long.",c="These are big tenderloins! You must have taken down some real monsters out there."},
[92685]={t="The Hills Have Eyes",o="Loot 7 Blood-Stained Bandit Masks from Highwayman Bandits in the Gustberry Lowlands.",d="The bandits have camps all over and there's a small one in the hills just north of here. Head up there and start cracking skulls. If we can catch them off guard and take them out before they come for us, we might just even the odds enough to stand a chance.\n\nBring me their masks. The bloodier the better.",p="If you manage to bring me enough bandit masks, maybe I'll stitch a blanket out of them and give it to Ferauu.\n\n<Aamelia laughs loudly.>",c="When I said the bloodier the better, you really listened. Good. It lets me know you made it hurt.\n\nOn a serious note, thank you for what you've done so far. I've been floating aimlessly around this farm for weeks as if I was just waiting for the end to come. I think I'm starting to have hope again.\n\nFerauu and his thugs are due any time now. All that's left is to go out and face them. What do you say, will you see this through to the end with me?"},
[92693]={t="Standing Our Ground",o="Speak with Aamelia Windfield when you are ready to confront the bandit leader.",d="You've done a lot to give us a fighting chance. Even if we die today, we'll at least know we gave it our best shot.\n\nThis is your last chance, stranger. If you want to head back to Valanaar and live another day, I wouldn't blame you.\n\nOn the other hand, if you really have a thing for lost causes just let me know when you are ready to go. We'll walk out there with our heads held high and whatever happens, happens.",p="There's not enough stormapples in skywall to repay you for this.",c="I... can't believe it's over. I need to stop and calm myself before my heart leaps right out of my chest."},
[92698]={t="What Is My Purpose?",o="Speak with Aamelia Windfield about the Malfunctioning Cyclone Construct.",d="<You lean in close to try and hear the words coming from beneath the giant construct's armor plates.>\n\n...Function error...\n\n...Question...\n\n...What is....\n\n...Function...\n\n<These fragmented words and phrases seem to just repeat. Maybe someone nearby knows more about this construct?>",c="The construct? It's been wandering around the fields for decades. Since the wind elementals left us, I think. Alvarion suspected that it used to haul harvests to market, or maybe tend to livestock back before this was an orchard. That could have been a thousand years ago though.\n\nIn the old days, the Windshapers used to maintain these constructs. We've talked about petitioning them to come and take a look at it, but it's never been a pressing concern to us. Mostly we just ignore it these days."},
[92700]={t="The Grand Skyseer",o="Find Ayessa Dawnsinger in Valanaar.",d="Now that you've arrived in Valanaar, you'll likely want to check in with the other members of the Windshapers here. The current Grand Skyseer and her people operate out of the lodge near the center of Valanaar.\n\nYou should also be aware, the Windshapers and High Order don't get along very well in these parts. Be careful and give the High Order a good, wide berth. We've got enough to worry about with the cult, I won't tolerate faction violence in the streets of Valanaar.",c="Elder Amberwind sent me a message about you and your exploits in Shen'dar Village. You are most welcome here, friend.\n\nYou have a strong aura, and you clearly have a resonance with the spirits. Fewer and fewer of us have the skysight of late, and Zephras needs those with the gift if we are to survive these trying times. I am glad you have found your way to me.\n\nI look forward to further making your acquaintance."},
[92703]={t="Deliver the News",o="Speak with Alvarion Windfield in Valanaar.",d="I guess it doesn't feel quite right to keep calling you stranger after all of this so... thank you, $N. \n\nIf you wouldn't mind and are back out that way, please let Alvarion know what happened here. Also, tell him that once he's up on his feet he needs to bring a windshaper back here to look at that construct for us to make sure it's safe to have around our... our family.\n\n<Aamelia touches her belly gently.>\n\nHe doesn't know about this part. Let's just keep that bit between us for now.",c="<Alvarion's eyes tear up as you finish retelling the story of what happened at the orchard.>\n\nI don't know how to thank you, friend. I came to Valanaar looking for hope. A vain hope, I was almost certain. But instead I found a hero. A real hero, like the stories from before we came to Skywall. \n\nI'll never forget what you did for us, $N. You'll always be welcome at the Windfield home."},
[92706]={t="WANTED: Bruuz",o="Bring Bruuz's Dorsal Fin to Gazlowe in Ratchet.",d="Calling all anglers!\n\nA giant shark has been circling the waters near the shipping dock, attacking sailors and small boats. Dockworkers have given it the nickname \"Bruuz\". A hefty reward will be given to whoever brings me its fin!\n\n-- Gazlowe"},
[92708]={t="A Grand Adventure",o="Listen to what Ayessa Dawnsinger has to say.",d="The Windshapers have been hard at work trying to respond to the current crisis on Zephras Isle. We have made several surprising discoveries in our search for the missing wind spirits, and we are developing a plan of action that could help us gain the means to save the island.\n\nWe'll need strong young adventurers like yourself for this to work however. Please, if you have a moment, let us speak on this further.",c="So now you see? There is a world of knowledge and untapped potential outside of Skywall. This will never stop being our home, but I've come to believe that the path to our salvation lies below. We must travel to Azeroth and gain the power and means to save Zephras Isle. This is the way.\n\nWill you have the courage to join us when the time comes?"},
[92871]={t="In Service of Zephras",o="Report to Valennia Stormfist and let her know that the Windshapers are with them in their fight against the Al'Aketh.",d="Valennia Stormfist and her peacekeepers have ever been the protectors of Zephras, and we've done our best to lend aid where we can. There are rumors of larger-scale cult movements around the island, and they are clearly gearing up for something.\n\nReport to Valennia and reiterate to her that the Windshapers offer their full support in Valanaar's efforts against the Al'Aketh, should the need arise.",c="You seem eager to lend aid immediately. Come, let's speak further on the current situation."},
[92880]={t="Return to Valanaar",o="Bring Yorna's Report to Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar.",d="I suspect it will take a bit of time for us to mop up what's left of the attackers, but our chances are far better now. Head back to Valanaar and let them know that we are stable here now.\n\nI can't thank you enough for your help. We'd be in much worse shape without you. I asked for reinforcements and it seems that I got a burgeoning hero instead. I'll take that.\n\nMay the four winds bless you, $C.",c="<Valennia looks visibly relieved as you tell her about the status of the eastern watchtower.>\n\nThank the winds."},
[92881]={t="The High Elder's Request",o="Speak with Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.",d="The attacks on both the western and eastern watchtowers are not a coincidence. Based on what you told us about what occurred at the western watchtower with that skypriest, our best guess is that the cult is trying to do something to the anchor pylons.\n\nPlease speak with High Elder Shadowsong. He will tell you about a lead that could prove to be promising.",c="I have a small matter that requires just the kind of assistance that an adventurer like yourself can provide."},
[92947]={t="Making Our Move",o="Slay 7 Al'Aketh Guardians, 7 Al'Aketh Spiritcallers, and 7 Al'Aketh Blademasters, then report to Hyusaa Quickbreeze at the Shrine of Akir.",d="Everyone is here, good. I've just sent a few of my best fighters in through the front of the shrine to cause a bit of trouble and serve as a distraction, while I lead the the bulk of our forces in from the flank.\n\nIf all goes well, we should be able to punch through quickly and take out the High Priestess. As for you, get in there and start cracking skulls. Meet my second, Hyusaa Quickbreeze, near the steps to the shrine after you've caused some trouble.\n\nWinds guide you, $C.",c="We fought hard to get this far but it isn't over yet."},
[93036]={t="Infiltrating the Cult",o="Speak with Sania Silverstream in Shen'dar Village.",d="You may or may not be aware of this, but Sania Silverstream over there is a \"missionary\" for the Al'Aketh. They like to play at being a normal religious order and send non-threatening emissaries around to recruit. We've tolerated Sania so far to avoid direct conflict with the cult, but it's obvious the illusion of peace won't last much longer.\n\nYou are new here and unknown to most, so I'd like to see if you can use Sania to get close to the cult and find out what their plans are for the village.",c="Greetings child, my name is Sania Silverstream and I am a junior priestess in the Order of the Al'Aketh. Do you wish to learn more of our sovereign, the Windlord Al'Akir?\n\nThere is always room at the Windlord's table for the righteous and the repentant."},
[93065]={t="Prepare for Battle",o="Speak with Valennia Stormfist in the Gustberry Lowlands.",d="The Peacekeepers are mobilizing and we are all gearing up to head out. Make whatever preparations you need to make and meet us at the eastern road leading north out of town. We'll have one final check-in with everyone before we move out.",c="We are as ready as we'll ever be."},
[93090]={t="What Comes Next",o="Speak with Ayessa Dawnsinger when you are prepared to leave Zephras Isle.",d="Please extend my thanks to Ayessa for all that the Windshapers and your new friends from this \"Earthen Ring\" have done for Zephras Isle. I'm aware of the plan to take the Windshapers' shamans and leave the island, and your order has my blessing and well-wishes in this expedition.\n\nI can only hope that whatever solution the Windshapers find can truly provide us with the stability we've lacked these past years.\n\nWinds be with you, $N.",c="I'm pleased to hear that we have High Elder Shadowsong's blessing for our expedition. Now that the cult has been defeated and preparations have been made, I think it's finally time.\n\nMuln has worked diligently to help us get stable skycutter transport going between Zephras Isle and a place called Mulgore, where the Earthen Ring make their home. We've been doing test voyages and some of our people are already waiting on the other side."},
[93159]={t="The Strange Hermit",o="Speak with the Strange Hermit in the Shadowgale Forest and learn more about him.",d="Uh, um... h-hello, I mean to say, hi! Greetings, even! I'm sorry... it's um, been so long since I've actually spoken to another person. I'm afraid I'm a bit rusty at this.\n\n<The strange hooded figure shifts uncomfortably before you.>\n\nSo er, um... how is your day going?",c="...that's about all I have to say about it. I was--um--somewhere else before I was here. Now I'm here and I have my friends, and my things. T-things I built, I mean. That's about all I need. I think that's all I need, anyway.\n\nI have to say though, it is nice to talk to someone who will talk back. The forest spirits try, but they just end up singing at me. That's nice in its own way, but not exactly s-stimulating conversation."},
[93160]={t="The Forest's Bounty",o="Gather 8 Shadowgale Acorns in Shadowgale Forest.",d="I do appreciate you stopping by to talk with me! I-If you do want to help out, I could use a bit of help gathering up acorns from the forest floor. I've gathered most of the ones close by but there sure are a lot of raptor-bird things in the forest. It's dangerous out there and I'd rather not become a giant bird's lunch!\n\nSo if you want, you could maybe gather them for me? I'll make us something tasty if you do!",p="Mmm, I think you are going to like what I can cook up with these acorns!",c="Thank you, stranger! You'll find that these are delicious once roasted! \n\nPlease excuse me, it won't take me long to whip this up."},
[93165]={t="Mercy Falls on Deaf Ears",o="Collect 5 Al'Aketh Cultist's Ears from the Al'Aketh cultists in Shadowgale Forest, the Shrine of Akir, or Gustberry Lowlands.",d="The Al'Aketh have visited great tragedy upon our enclave, and blood must be repaid with blood.\n\nI have an offer for you, stranger. Should you find conflict with these accursed cultists, bring me the ears of those you kill. I will reward you for each that you return with in both coin and, in time, access to the Nightclaw's secrets should you prove yourself to be a true friend.",p="I will not rest until my fangs have gone through the throat of every single cultist on this isle.",c="Excellent work. Only good things can happen by eliminating the cult. Hopefully this sends a message that the Nightclaw are not to be trifled with and that our resentments run deep.\n\nI suspect you have your work cut out for yourself, taking on the cult. If you gather more ears, bring them here."},
[93172]={t="Free the Hollows",o="Destroy 10 Wind Hollows in Shadowgale Forest.",d="Most of the elves on this island seem to think that these woods are haunted, and they aren't wrong.\n\nAt the old ruins to the northeast, a strange type of ghost-like spirits gather. Some nights, you can almost hear them \"singing\". It's not like any song I've heard before, but it's definitely a song and it's... just so sad.\n\nI'm not sure why, but I think something terrible happened there at some point, and the spirits are trapped there somehow. If you are feeling brave, maybe you can help set them free?",c="Thank you, stranger."},
[93317]={t="Crab Season",o="Collect 6 pieces of Windsong Crawler Meat.",d="Are you familiar with Windsong Crawlers? You see, these crabs are native only to Windsong Lake here on Zephras, and they are only able to be harvested a few weeks of the year.\n\nWith all of the cult activity of late, I've not been able to get out to the lake to harvest them, and our window is rapidly closing. I'd be appreciative if you could go and gather some for me. They can generally be found along the shorelines around the lake and in rivers.\n\nDo be careful though, they are meaner than they look!",p="Windsong Crawler meat is common enough here but it was something of a delicacy on the islands of Anvilas and Siroccas. Was a time, back when the skystreams were open that the locals would mob me for the stuff when I'd make the trip to Shen'dramar or New Eldre'naar.\n\nNot been able to visit those places in... well... a long time.",c="Winds bless me, this meat looks fantastic! \n\nThank you so much, $C."},
[93318]={t="WANTED: Vulgara the Insatiable",o="Kill Vulgara the Insatiable in the Shen'dar Highlands and bring her head to Danarii Bellowveil.",d="By order of Constable Aonda of the Peacekeepers, a bounty is hereby placed upon the scourge of the highlands, Vulgara the Insatiable. Last spotted on a hilltop rise just southwest of Shen'dar Village, the winged vuldren terror is highly dangerous and should be approached with caution.\n\nDeliver the beast's head to Danarii Bellowveil to receive your reward.",p="I'll need the creature's head as proof of the deed.",c="If we didn't have enough on our plates between the cult and the highlands bandits, we don't need a giant vuldren terrorizing our citizens as well. You've done a great thing here today. As promised, here is your reward."},
[93319]={t="Pilfered Windstones",o="Collect 10 Pilfered Windstones from the Highlands Bandits in the Shen'dar Highlands.",d="We are relying on windstones more and more for day-to-day living here on Zephras so we try and maintain a cache of them in reserve for emergencies. Lately I've noticed some go missing from our stores.\n\nWe've found windstones on bandits we've captured recently, and I suspect they are behind our shortages.\n\nIf you find yourself near the bandit cave to the north, mind knocking a few heads together and reclaiming some of our pilfered windstones for me?",p="These sneakthieves have likely been breaking into our supplies for months. I tried to convince Aonda to put a raid together to clear out that bandit cave for good, but she didn't want to pull the few peacekeepers we have away from the village. \n\nWith the cultists at Falaath Village to the south growing in numbers, I suppose I can't fault her for that.",c="Thanks shaman. This should help us get by for now. If we can't get the supply routes squared away soon though, a few stolen windstones will be the least of our worries."},
[93320]={t="Tower Defense",o="Report to Yorana Windyreed at the eastern watchtower in the Gustberry Lowlands.",d="I've just received word that the cult is attacking the pylon watchtower just outside of town! I've sent the few extra peacekeepers we have here to try and break through the enemy back line to relieve the defenders, but any additional help could mean the difference between our people there living or dying.\n\nPlease leave immediately for the east watchtower and provide whatever aid you can.\n\nMy lieutenant Yorana Windyreed led the relief force. If she still lives she can tell you how best to help.",c="We are holding them off for now, but they have greater numbers and our fighters are starting to get tired. We need to do something to break the stalemate, and do it fast."},
[93459]={t="More Al'Aketh Ears",p="<Vayn nods at you.>"},
[93552]={t="Harvesting Windstones",o="Collect 15 Windstone Clusters from Raw Windstones in Thendal Grove.",d="Windstones are a critical resource on Zephras Isle as they contain the raw, concentrated energy of the winds themselves. The wind elementals who used to live here on Zephras with us vanished a number of years ago, and since then, the magic that sustains this island is slowly fading. Not without limitations, the windstones are still a reliable energy source, and are incredibly valuable to us.\n\nYou'll find raw windstones scattered around the grove. Think you can help me harvest them?",p="Hello there, $C.",c="Thank you very much for these. As elves we all have a deep connection to magic and these windstones are becoming more and more precious as the magic imbued into this island by the great anchor pylons continues to fade. \n\nWindstones aren't the only beneficial thing you can harvest from the land. Please, take one of these manuals."},
[93735]={t="The Broken Construct",o="Find Riaani Nightwind on the west side of Valanaar.",d="Historically, the Windshapers have seen to the tending of the magical instruments and devices that were gifted to us by the spirits of the wind. This includes the myriad of magical constructs around the island. Since the spirits left us, only a scant few of these are still functional.\n\nOne of the few remaining working constructs in Valanaar has become damaged. One of our artisans was dispatched to help, but he may be in need of aid. Travel to the west end of the city and offer any assistance you can.",c="<Riaani's face is buried under the heaving armor plates of the construct, attempting to work on the mechanisms underneath. He does not notice your presence at all.>\n\nStorms curse--where is the core?! Who thought it would be a good idea to remove the Gyrozephyr as well? It's a miracle this construct's winds haven't dissipated entirely by now!"},
[93736]={t="Unwelcome Spirits",o="Gather 10 Wind Hollow Essences from Wind Hollows in the Shadowgale Forest.",d="The paramount concern of the Windshapers is to better understand why the spirits left us, and what we may be able to do to bring them back. One curious fixture of Shadowgale Forest to the north is the presence of a curious form of wind sprite that some call \"hollows\". We know little of them and why they are there, but we do know that they first started to appear after the spirits of the wind left us.\n\nI need you to go there and disperse them. Gather the remains and bring them back here.",p="Shadowgale Forest is a dangerous place. Some even say it's haunted. I'm quite sure that I don't believe that, but I do know that it's not for the faint hearted, or the unprepared.",c="Handling these essences fills me with a sense of... deep disquiet. I can almost feel a malevolent, regretful aura emanating from them. It's enough to make me faint.\n\n<Endaria shudders slightly.>\n\nI do not look forward to studying these further."},
[93737]={t="The Broken Construct",o="Speak with Riaani Nightwind and listen to what he has to say.",d="Oh, hello. Ayessa sent you to assist me? Very well then. \n\nNot sure what an obvious novice like yourself can do, but if you give me a moment to pull my head out of this construct's innards I might have a few ideas of things you can do to help.",p="I can't imagine why anyone would want to steal these components from this construct. Other than the gyrozephyr these components have almost no practical application. Even the gyro would be nigh-useless outside of its intended purpose.",c="Thank you for scavenging these materials. I imagine that some of this wasn't terribly easy to get. \n\nWith these parts I can get the construct up and running again. From there we can just hope that its memory is intact and it can tell us who took its components."},
[93738]={t="The Broken Construct",o="Report back to Ayessa Dawnsinger in Valanaar.",d="Brightwish, eh? So the High Order wanted to remove these components for some reason. But why though?\n\nThe High Order has always been meddlesome, constantly wanting to experiment with the wind spirits' magic. They are too bold by a mile, and we've strictly forbidden them from meddling with knowledge under Windshaper purview, but lately they've been testing our patience.\n\nI think you should report what you've learned back to Ayessa Dawnsinger. She can instruct you further on what to do.",c="Very interesting, so it was the High Order that was responsible for the construct breaking down?\n\nI know Belathaan. He's Valennia Stormfist's cousin and his mother was actually a Windshaper. It's disappointing that he was involved in this.\n\nI need to reflect on this for a moment."},
[93739]={t="Exploring the Horde",o="Speak with Nazgrel in Grommash Hold to receive further instructions. Use the instructions received to locate and speak with Vol'jin, Cairne Bloodhoof, and Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",d="Azeroth is a large world, and the territory of the Horde is vast. The Undercity, Orgrimmar, and Thunder Bluff all have very unique people and culture.\n\nIf you are to be a guest of the Horde here on Azeroth, it would do you good to visit each of our capital cities in turn. Speak with my advisor Nazgrel for directions.",c="So you have returned. I hope that you learned much in your journey.\n\nIt is my understanding that your people are still establishing themselves in Mulgore. While you wait for them, I'd encourage you to explore the territory around Orgrimmar. The Barrens in particular is always in need of eager adventurers like yourself."},
[93740]={t="Blood for Blood",o="Collect 10 Al'Aketh Windstone Charms from the corpses of Al'Aketh cultists in the Gustberry Lowlands.",d="A number of our Windshaper novices were found dead in the Highlands this morning. We can't be certain but there is a strong chance that the Al'Aketh are responsible. Windshapers trade blood for blood, every time.\n\nHead north and kill any Al'Aketh you encounter. Bring me their windstone prayer charms as proof of the deed. We do not forgive and we do not forget.",p="The Al'Aketh have engaged in their bloody zealotry for far too long. This is only the start of the reckoning they face.",c="<Ayessa looks shaken and distant as you hand her the windstone charms.>\n\nDon't mind me, $N. Today has merely been... a trying day. Thank you for your service to the windshapers thus far."},
[93746]={t="A Firm Response",o="Confront Belathaan Brightwish along the road to the Shrine of Akir.",d="The High Order has been warned of the consequences of meddling with the Windshaper's affairs. I think we need to make an example out of Belathaan and send him back to the High Order with a few bruises and a healthy respect for the boundaries we set.\n\nBelathaan was seen leaving town, traveling north towards the Shrine of Akir. I don't know why he was going there, but confronting him alone on the road is the safest option. Find him, and put a bit of fear into his heart.",c="Wait--what?! Belathaan... is dead? \n\n<Ayessa listens as you give your account of what occurred.> \n\nThe High Order was meeting with the Al'Aketh to discuss peace? There is no peace with the cult, they are murderous zealots. What was Elaadrin thinking sending Belathaan to treat with them alone?\n\nPay this no mind, $N. You are not at fault for this. The arrogance of the High Order is to blame, yet again. You were merely in the right place at the wrong time."},
[93836]={t="The Fate of Zephras",o="Speak with Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.",d="Muln has told me much of the elemental lords and I am afraid that we have good reason to fear Al'Akir. Now that the wards that have hidden Zephras from his view are down, we are utterly defenseless. If he chooses to attack us, we stand no chance against him here in his own domain.\n\nHigh Elder Shadowsong needs to know of the danger we are in, and more importantly, what our intentions are for our mission to Azeroth. We will find the means to save our home. I swear it.",c="<Talaanis Shadowsong listens intently as you tell him of what transpired above the Shrine of Akir, and of Ayessa's plan to leave Zephras Isle.>\n\nI need to reflect on this further, but looking at the upside, we have rid ourselves of Lorthuna and deprived the cult of their leader. Our home has not been invaded yet and on the timeline of elemental gods, it could be years... decades even, before Al'Akir deigns to turn his attention to us.\n\nThere is much to fear now, but much to celebrate as well."},
[93926]={t="The Western Watch",o="Find Peacekeeper Vaaniel at the western watchtower.",d="Whatever reason the cult has for attacking the tower, it's not worth losing our people over.\n\nI'd like for you to head to the southwest and check in on that watchtower for us. Find the peacekeepers there and tell them to head back to the village. Holding that tower is not worth the lives it would cost and I'd rather concentrate the defenders we do have here to protect our citizens.\n\nPeacekeeper Vaaniel is in charge; let him know to head back here as quickly as possible. Hurry!",c="<The body here is somewhat fresh, clearly only recently having been killed. Judging by the burns and scorch marks on this peacekeeper's skin, it's clear that they were killed by the cult's storm-wielding spellcasters.>"},
[93927]={t="A Last Request",o="Collect the note you found near the dead peacekeeper and read it to determine your next steps.",d="<As you inspect the body of the dead peacekeeper, a bloody note falls free of his hands. Picking it up and reading it may give you a clue as to how to proceed from here.>",p="What news from the western watch?",c="So they are all dead, then. Storms curse these cult bastards!\n\nWhile you managed to take out the priest and stop the cultists at the tower, I confess that I'm now doubly concerned about whatever it was you said that they were doing to the pylon. The fact that there was such a massive cache of windstones there with them tells me that they needed enormous energy for it.\n\nI have to wonder, what's the end goal here? Violating the pylon, attacking the village? To what end?"},
[93948]={t="Deliver the Signet",o="Deliver the Shadowsong Family Signet to Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.",d="Since you are going to Valanaar anyway, please deliver the signet ring you recovered from the tower to Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar. \n\nHe will want this back, and more importantly, he will want to learn the fate of his nephew. Talaanis is the High Elder of Zephras Isle and more importantly, he is a good man who is well loved by the people, despite our current hardships. It pains me to think of how he will react to this news. Please express my condolences for his loss.",p="What is that you have for me? Oh... oh no.",c="I... am very sorry to hear that my nephew is dead. I thank you kindly for recovering this, and bringing it to me.\n\nIt's not common that such capable young shen'dorei come down from the highlands. If you need work, please speak with Valennia Stormfist, the captain of the peacekeepers here in Valanaar. These days we need all the help we can get."},
[93949]={t="Bugged",o="Kill Skyhoppers in Valanaar until you've eliminated 8 Enchanted Skyhoppers.",d="We've been bugged.\n\nIt's skyhopper season in the lowlands, which means the pests are everywhere. One of the High Order mages reported that one of the insects that they killed had an enchantment of some kind placed upon it. When we inspected it closely it seems to be some sort of listening spell.\n\nWe suspect that the cult is using these enchanted insects as spies. Go and exterminate them for us. You won't be able to tell which are enchanted by looking at them, so you'll just have to kill them all.",c="I'm sure there are more of these critters around Valanaar, but every enchanted skyhopper we stomp out makes the city just a tiny bit safer."},
[93951]={t="A Little Beauty",o="Collect 8 Hippogryph Down feathers in the Shen'dar Highlands.",d="The hippogryphs that have taken up residence southwest of the village can be a nuisance, but they also present a rather unique opportunity to obtain their feathers. Many skyborne love to adorn their hair with vibrant plumes and the down feathers of a hippogryph are exceptionally vibrant and, more importantly, silky soft.\n\nIf you are heading that way, try and gather as many of the fallen feathers as you can from around their nesting grounds. Do be careful, as wild hippogryph are not tolerant of guests.",p="What beautiful things did you bring me?",c="It might seem a bit of a vain triviality, gathering feathers for our hair. However, even in times like these, one needs to embrace the small joys as much as possible. \n\nIf one thing I create brings someone joy, then I will consider that to be a good day. Thank you for bringing me these and helping me bring some joy to Zephras."},
[93958]={t="The Inner Sanctum",o="Speak with Valennia Stormfist inside the inner sanctum at the Shrine of Akir.",d="Valennia's forces just breached the inner sanctum. The fighting was thick in there at first, but it's grown... unsettlingly quiet. Go in there and do your best to link up with Valennia and her forces... if any of them are left.\n\nI'll stay here and watch your back.",c="<Valennia looks gravely wounded.>"},
[94411]={t="Meddlesome Mages",o="Slay 6 High Order Apprentices in Shen'dar Highlands.",d="Be warned, members of the High Order have been seen in the vicinity of the standing stones north of the village. We have warned them time and again to not meddle at our sacred sites, but they are growing more bold in pushing us. Prove your resolve to us by going to the standing stones and dispersing them.\n\nI am loathe to condone outright bloodshed, but do what you must to drive them off. Return to me when it's done.",c="Direct conflict with our shen'dorei brothers and sisters only weakens us as a people, but decisive action must at times be taken to prevent greater tragedy.\n\nThe mages of the High Order have zero regard for the consequences of their magical meddling. The forces that bind our island are fragile and vulnerable and all it could take is one thoughtless action to destroy our home."},
[94414]={t="The Anchors of Zephras",o="Speak with Halaan Hawk-Eye and borrow his gift to view the anchor pylon in the distance.",d="Greetings, young $N. I oftentimes come here to look upon the ancient anchor pylon. Gifts from the spirits of the winds, they bind and sustain our island. Of late however, their magic has grown unstable and inconsistent.\n\nThey suffer no distress I can see. Their splendor has not changed.\n\nIf you'd like, I can lend you my gift to look upon them yourself.",c="Thank you for taking a moment to share this with me. I will continue to watch over the grove, and ponder on the state of our homeland."},
[94484]={t="Unnerving Silence",o="Find and speak with Elegael Thornpaw in the northeastern part of Shadowgale Forest.",d="A moment if you will, $N. Are you headed towards Shadowgale Forest? There is a druid conclave there in a cave to the northeast. I have been waiting on word from them but their correspondence is long overdue.\n\nWith Ban'aethall in ruins and all the unrest lately I worry something dire may have happened. Please, if you are able, go seek out Elegael Thornpaw and put my mind at ease.",c="Thank goodness our message got to Lotheluum. Wait, where are the rest of the reinforcements? Surely it is not just you they sent?\n\n<Elegael pales as you relay your conversation with Lotheluum.>\n\nSo the message did not get through. We are in dire straits indeed then.\n\nIt seems we must handle this on our own. Time is of the essence."},
[94485]={t="Tears of the Lady",o="Collect 8 Lady's Tear Moss.",d="If we are to save my fellows in the Nightclaw Den, I am going to need some ingredients for a poultice. The first and most important is a spindly moss called Lady's Tear. It typically grows on the base of the trees here in Shadowgale.\n\nThis moss secretes a sticky substance that acts as an antiseptic and is perfect for binding open wounds. I have gathered what little I can reach but I know there is more in this forest.\n\nGo and be swift. We are going to need a lot if the injured I left behind still live.",p="Have you found the Lady's Tear?",c="<Elegael takes the sticky mound of moss from you with a weak smile.>\n\nThank you, $N, you have done well. This is exactly what we need."},
[94486]={t="Feathers for Binding",o="Collect 20 feathers from the Shadowgale Shrieklings in Shadowgale Forest.",d="The other ingredient I need for the poultice is feathers from the Shadowgale shrieklings that roam this forest. In their juvenile form, the shrieklings have insulative feathers which would be ideal to put over the moss. These feathers will prevent the antiseptic sap from drying out and will provide at least some protection against the elements.\n\nBe warned, the shrieklings are normally docile but they have been incredibly hostile of late. Their large talons can easily disembowel you if you aren't careful.",p="It deeply saddens me to ask you to kill the young shrieklings, but with the rise in their aggression it is for the best. We can only handle so many emergencies at a time.",c="Thank you for these. I will be sure to use every feather so their sacrifice will not be in vain."},
[94487]={t="Unwanted and Unworthy",o="Collect 10 Bloodied Heirlooms from Al'Aketh Footsoldiers and Al'Aketh Stormchasers in the Shadowgale Forest.",d="The Al'Aketh Cultists ambushed us with no warning, though their motives remain a mystery to me. I knew these cultists had clouds between their ears, but I never imagined they would upset the delicate balance here on Zephras with such brutality. Go, slay as many as you can and take their heirlooms if they wear any.\n\n<Elegael spits.>\n\nThese storm-cursed cultists don't deserve to be called shen'dorei. The beasts of the forest can have their bodies. Their ashes don't deserve the winds.",p="I will make the cult pay for every drop of druid blood they have spilled this day.",c="<Elegael looks down at the collection of bloodied heirlooms with distress.>\n\nSo many young lives with so much potential now gone forever. Thank you for returning these, $C.\n\nI will hold onto them for safekeeping until I am able to take them to the High Elder. There they can go back into the collection and await the next and perhaps more worthy generation to come of age."},
[94488]={t="The Ties That Bind",o="Kill Commander Haalien and bring his head to Elegael Thornpaw in the Shadowgale Forest.",d="The reason for cultists' presence here still baffles me, but I smell a familiar scent over the bloodshed.\n\nOne of our circle druids, Haalien, disappeared months back. It appears he's thrown his sorry hide in with the cultists.\n\nShow him what happens when he spills the blood of his kin! Take his head and return it to me.",p="Are our brethren's lives truly worth so little to you, Haalien?",c="<Elegael grimaces at the severed head, but nods curtly.>\n\nThank you, $N. No matter how much rage I have within me, it would have been difficult to strike down my own cousin.\n\nDo not mourn for him. His ignorance and malice has killed many innocents this day."},
[94489]={t="The Wounds of Betrayal",o="Enter the Nightfang Den and heal 7 druids and find Jorel Windsinger in Shadowgale Forest.",d="I have finished the poultices. Quickly, take them to the druids in the cave, north just across the clearing. I know my brethren are in much more dire condition than I. They are likely too injured to heal their own wounds. There are so few of us shen'dorei druids that every life is precious.\n\nBefore you go, I have a selfish request. My mate, Jorel Windsinger was in dire condition when I left. Please, see to his wounds if he still lives.",c="<Elegael's face pales as you relay the fate of Jorel and the condition of the rest of the druids.>\n\nNo... no! This is far worse than I had--\n\n<Elegael chokes back a sob and grits her teeth, letting out a pained snarl.>\n\nThey will pay. They will ALL pay. Anyone who allies with the Al'Aketh will feel my wrath! This I swear."},
[94490]={t="Ripped Missive",o="Bring the Ripped Missive to Elegael Thornpaw in the Shadowgale Forest.",d="<Tucked behind one of Haalien's bracers is a note that's been slightly torn and bloodstained in your fight. It looks like it contains useful information about the cultist motivations for the attack on the druid den. Elegael would be interested in this intel.>",c="They were here for the pylon? But to what end? We were not the original reason for their attack?\n\n<Elegael trails off shaking with rage as she reads.>\n\nThey murdered my people because we were an inconvenience! I shall tear apart every cultist with my fangs! I will make sure none leave this place with their lives.\n\nGo, swiftly! If the orders truly originated in Valanaar, it means it is likely a traitor hiding there. Give the missive to Lotheluum in Valanaar and tell him what has transpired."},
[94491]={t="The Fate of the Den",o="Give the missive to Lotheluum in Valanaar and tell him what has transpired.",d="It would appear that there is a correspondent hiding somewhere in Valanaar feeding information to the cult. I am clearly in no shape to make the journey, but Lotheluum needs to know what transpired here.\n\nHe should also know the fate of those who are no longer with us. Thanks to your help I think we can handle the rest of the situation from here, though the damage has been done.\n\nPlease go swiftly, $N. I hope our paths will cross again someday. Until then, I have cultists to slay.",c="<Lotheluum wears a look of genuine terror as you recount the events from the druid den.>\n\nI--I'm sorry, $N. I need just a moment. There are no words I possess that can describe the loss.\n\nThis is grave news indeed. If this missive is not fabricated, then we indeed have at best an accomplice and at worst a traitor here in Valanaar. I will take this to the High Elder immediately! I will not let my fellows' sacrifice be in vain."},
[94568]={t="The Cult's True Plans",o="Speak with Talaanis Shadowsong and observe the conversation.",d="The turncoat clearly was afraid of what the cult had planned, enough so to defect and seek our aid. It's truly unfortunate that he is dead and took his secrets to the grave with him.\n\nWe must discuss this further to determine our next steps.",c="We could try and send peacekeepers to directly engage the cult forces, but we would not fare well against them in open battle.\n\nWe are going to need a different approach."},
[94896]={t="Aid For The Refugees",o="Collect 8 Abandoned Belongings from the ruins of Ban'aethal.",d="You look like a capable adventurer. Do you happen to be headed towards Shadowgale Forest? Ban'aethal lies deep in the forest; that's where we're all from.\n\n<Ealaane gestures to the other refugees.>\n\nWe've recently had to evacuate Ban'aethal, as it began to fall into the sky. It was sudden and in the middle of the night. If you are headed that way, would you please look for any belongings left behind? The forest and village are far too dangerous for us to return to now.",p="So many of us left with nothing more than the clothes on our backs. Any belongings you might recover would be cherished.",c="Thank you, $C, you have done a great kindness to us refugees this day. I will make sure to return these to their owners. At least it gives us a place to start over from."},
[94897]={t="The Fate of a Loved One",o="Find Resaan in the Ruins of Ban'aethal.",d="If you are traveling to Ban'aethal, I have a selfish request. My love, Resaan... I believe is no longer a part of this world. He had tried to go back to get supplies even though I begged him to stay. It has been over a week already and I fear the worst.\n\nPlease, if you find him, bring him home. If he has perished then I beg you to please bring me his heirloom.",p="Have you any news of Resaan? Please, $C, the wait is hard to endure after everything that has happened.",c="<Ealaane's eyes well with tears.>\n\nOh, Resaan my love. What will become of us now? There was so much... it feels as if our lives together had just started.\n\nThank you, $C. The world is cruel to take both my home and my love from me. At least his heirloom will give me some closure."},
[95204]={t="Crest of Lordaeron",o="Bring the Crest of Lordaeron to Oran Snakewrithe in Undercity.",d="<A weathered crest depicting the mark of Lordaeron. With so few relics left after the kingdom's fall, someone in the Undercity would be very keen to get their hands on this.>",p="What have you got there, $C? A tasty morsel?",c="<Oran bites the crest to ensure authenticity.>\n\nWell I'll be. A genuine relic of our home. Mostly intact, too. We need to be extra careful with this one.\n\nThank you for your aid in restoring our history, $C. I'll see to it that we take good care of this."},
[95216]={t="The New Plague",o="Collect the Highly Toxic Strain from Witherfang in Ruins of Lordaeron for Theodore Griffs in Undercity.",d="Welcome to the most vital organ of the Undercity: The Apothecarium! Here we experiment on the most virulent of Azeroth's exotic specimens.\n\nYou've caught me in a good mood, so I will let you in on my latest investigation. It appears there is a particularly venomous arthropod stalking the ruins above our fair city. Its toxins are said to eat through even undead flesh. How exhilarating!\n\nI wish to validate these claims. Should you find yourself withering away from its bite, I should love a sample.",p="Any fool can tell you the most potent transmission method will always be through the blood.\n\nI must see this strain for myself!",c="You killed it??\n\nHmmph. Lucky for you this should be enough ichor to reverse engineer its properties. I would have expected more from a fellow alchemist.\n\nGet out of my sight!"},
[95349]={t="The Earthen Ring",o="Take the skycutter ship from Zephras Isle to Mulgore and speak with Alaana Stormwalker when you arrive.",d="The recent events with the cult have delayed my plans to travel to Azeroth and I must remain here in Valanaar for a time. You and a handful of other Windshapers will be our vanguard instead. Alaana Stormwalker will be waiting to receive our Windshapers upon arrival in Mulgore, and I'd encourage you to explore Azeroth while we finish our business here. We will join you soon.\n\nWhen you are ready, please proceed to the dock just outside this lodge and board the skycutter ship there. \n\nBanu-Alah, $N.",c="More adventurers from Zephras, I see. Wonderful. The winds surely favor us! It's going to take us some time to get ourselves established here, so you may want to take some time to explore this new land.\n\nAzeroth is an exciting new world, but it's also a dangerous world. You'd do well to prepare yourself for this new adventure by familiarizing yourself with the lands nearby."},
[95350]={t="Welcome to Azeroth",o="Travel to Orgrimmar and speak with Thrall in the Valley of Wisdom.",d="It's a big world down here, and our new allies are the key to our survival.\n\nThe Earthen Ring is a member of the \"Horde\", a proud collection of like-minded peoples. The nearby city of Thunder Bluff is a part of the Horde, and further to the east lies the capital of Orgrimmar.\n\nSeek out the flight master in the center of Thunder Bluff. They will fly you to Orgrimmar where you will make contact with the Horde warchief--Thrall, on behalf of the Windshapers. Winds guide you, $N.",c="Lok-tar, $C. I am Thrall, Warchief of the Horde.\n\nAn Earthen Ring messenger told me to expect members of the Windshapers, and here you are. I'd not have expected to see a high elf standing before me here in Orgrimmar, but the Horde will welcome you as our guest all the same.\n\nYou have my blessing to travel through Horde lands. Go with honor, Windshaper."},
[96101]={t="The Great Outdoors",o="Sit near Raan's Basic Campfire and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.",d="Greetings, $C. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\n\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\n\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.",c="So now that we've learned the basics, why don't you go and learn a tradeskill from the trainers in the village nearby. They will also teach you how to create a camp fixture suitable to your new profession."},
[96638]={t="The Adventurer",o="Speak to Raan Wildwind near Shen'dar Village.",d="More and more adventurers like yourself have been seeking glory and fortune outside of the safety of Thendal Grove. There's one such adventurer who has made a camp outside of Shen'dar Village, along the road leading southwest out of Thendal Grove.\n\nSeek him out and see what you can learn from him that may help you in your own travels.",c="Well met!"},
[96646]={t="Camping 101: Cooking",o="Speak with Zerril Softbreeze in Shen'dar Village to learn to become a cook.",d="So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, $C. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\n\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.",c="With this, you'll be able to set up a camp anywhere out in the wilderness. What you've learned is just the basics, so you won't be able to place too many furnishings around it.\n\nRaise your cooking skill and you might just be able to learn to make even bigger fires.\n\nYou can also learn the basics of furnishing your campsites from other tradeskill trainers if you're savvy in their skills."},
[97003]={t="Chol'aruk the Ravener",o="Bring the head of Chol'aruk to Gur'ak in the Barrens.",d="You there, $C. I need your aid. There are rumors of a beast that makes its lair deep in a cave at Thorn Hill, northeast of here. The Razormane call it Chol'aruk or \"The Ravener\". It's supposedly five times the size of a normal quilboar with a thirst for blood that can never be sated.\n\nMost don't believe the tales. But I do--because I've fought its like before.\n\nSeek out its lair and slay Chol'aruk. Bring me its head. I warn you though--prepare well and do not go alone.\n\nBlood and thunder, $C."},
[97242]={t="Yelmak's Medley",o="Take some cuttings from the Cattails and Speargrass growing around the water flows in the Valley of Honor and return to Kor'geld in Yelmak's Alchemy and Potions.",d="Yelmak doesn't want his apprentice breaking anything. Well, anything more than he already has.\n\nHe told me the young mixer in training has too much pride to ask for help when he really needs it. Yelmak wants to give him a taste of a particular home-brewed recipe.\n\nGather a mix of cattail and speargrass cuttings taken from the plants growing around the water in the Valley of Honor. I'd get them myself, but if I left the shop, Whuut would surely know we're catering to his mood.",p="We discover formulations and recipes by showing old ingredients to new generations, who experiment with them in their own way.",c="This type of cattail and speargrass is unique to Orgrimmar. Drinking from Azshara mountain spring water, and nourished by the sweat and blood soaked mineral dust of our rocky land, these herbs contain potent powers locked within.\n\nI'll give these to Yelmak, who may be able to win back Whuut's ear with a hands-on lesson."},
[97243]={t="Call of Fire",o="Bring the Torch of Dormant Flame to Olariaan Swiftburn at the Shrine of Flames in the Gustberry Lowlands.",d="Even though we are in the realm of Skywall, this is still the elemental plane. The spirits of all four elements speak to us, if we deign to listen. One among us Windshapers is in particular attunement with the element of fire. A shen'dorei by the name of Olariaan Swiftburn.\n\nBring this to him at the Shrine of Flames in the Gustberry Lowlands. You'll find it tucked away along the edge of the island, west of Valanaar.",p="Yes, $N? What do you have there?",c="So you've brought the torch. Yes, young $C, I can teach you to heed the call of fire. It will not be easy, but nothing that we do in this realm is ever easy."},
[97244]={t="Call of Fire",o="Slay Skypriest Faladiel in the Gustberry Lowlands and collect Faladiel's Heart.",d="There is an Al'Aketh Skypriest called Faladiel. He was once a caller of the flame and a stalwart Windshaper. Like so many Al'Aketh, he mortgaged his loyalty for power and his hands are now stained with the blood of his former brothers and sisters.\n\nYou will find Skypriest Faladiel at the farm to the northeast past Valanaar, just to the south of the Shrine of Akir. Kill the betrayer. Bring me his heart. It is a gruesome task, but it is needed for the ritual we are to perform.",p="The heart of a betrayer is a powerful reagent. The flames will eagerly accept such an offering and burn more intensely as it is consumed.",c="The Windshapers do not forget, and blood is always paid with blood. It pleases me that you were able to deliver this final, painful reminder of our creed to this traitor.\n\nThis heart will not be all that feeds the flames today, however. There is one other task that needs to be done."},
[97245]={t="Call of Fire",o="Find the home of Kuramaa in the Shen'dar Highlands, and defeat the spirit in combat. Bring Kuramaa's Mask to Olariaan Swiftburn in the Gustberry Lowlands when you are victorious.",d="The residents of the Shen'dar Highlands speak of an ancient forest sprite called Kuramaa. They say it lives inside of a twisted stump at the summit of a hill near the highlands Anchor Pylon.\n\nGo to the highlands and find this stump. Rap your fist upon the bark and Kuramaa will appear. Best the spirit in combat, and bring me its wooden mask.\n\nBe warned however, this entity will be exceptionally resistant to much of your magic. Only the touch of flame will lay low the spirit.",p="The spirit of Kuramaa is eternal, and it will manifest again when it is needed. Its mask is a source of great power, and will prove invaluable to the ritual we must complete.",c="We now have what we need. We will light the eternal flame and commune with the spirits of fire."},
[97246]={t="Meal Appeal",o="Visit Borstan's Firepit and tell him Thatog wants you to deliver Migi's lunch to him personally.",d="My son, Migi, always takes off to play with his friends all day. I tell him to pick up a lunch at Borstan's, but I know he almost never does, because he comes home starving. These kids think their games are more important than their own bodies!\n\nPlease, stop at Borstan's Firepit and tell him you're there to deliver Migi's lunch. You can almost certainly find Migi behind Grommash Hold with the rest of his friends.\n\nDuties keep me here during the day and I can't watch over his every meal.",c="Of course. Migi's parents and I have an arrangement to give Migi a bagged lunch every day, but I can only ensure the boy gets his food if he actually comes in to pick it up.\n\nSometimes, he doesn't pick up his meal multiple times a week, and I wonder where he gets the energy to stay out and play."},
[97249]={t="Favorite Food",o="Bring Migi's Lunch to him behind Grommash Hold.",d="Now that I know his parents worry about how much he's actually filling that belly, I've got an idea. \n\nThey made me promise not to pack the same meal every day, so Migi grows a taste for more than one thing. Still, whenever the smoker's full and we're making sweetglazed hog belly sandwiches, he always shows up for lunch. We've started crumbling the leftover crispy glazed bits as a topping--something we can add daily. \n\nTake this to him. Maybe he'll start showing up early and bringing friends!",p="I think we can win this one...",c="Borstan's Meats? Is that for one of us?\n\nOh!\n\nWow... this smells really good! Yummy.\n\nThanks for bringing me my lunch. I can tell what Borstan is going to be serving daily when my friends and I walk the road to Grommash Hold, by the smells alone. This tastes like my favorite, the sweetglaze! But it's different. I like the strong-flavored crumbs.\n\nIf it's going to be this tasty every day, I think we need to stop our game to take our lunch together!"},
[97253]={t="Parts and Pieces",o="Collect 5 Handfuls of Complicated Parts from the upper pirate camp south of Ratchet, then return to Wrenix the Wretched in Ratchet.",d="Hey, got a sec?\n\nSo, apparently, nobody I've sent to deal with the recent pirate problem has come back alive. After five or six attempts I thought, \"what if I sent a machine instead?\" Turns out, scimitars double as screwdrivers in a pinch, and before I could redirect it home, it was already in pieces and scattered across their camp!\n\nI need those parts back, and since this is a quick little retrieval mission, I'd wager your odds for survival are MUCH higher than the others. Whaddya say?"},
[97257]={t="Call of Fire",o="Wait for Olariaan to begin the ritual at the Brazier of Offering and follow his instructions.\n\nYou must deliver the Eternal Flame to Valanaar before the timer runs out.",d="Now we will perform the ritual. \n\nI will place the materials onto the altar and call forth the spirits of flame. If the offering is accepted, they will appear and light the Eternal Flame. You will then hold your torch forth and capture the flame.\n\nCarry the lit torch to Valanaar and place it in the Brazier of Eternal Flames. You must do so quickly, for the flames of the Firelands are quick to dissipate here in Skywall.",p="You have done well to come this far. You do the Windshapers honor, $N.",c="It is done. The Eternal Flame burns once again.\n\nYour trial is now complete. I am pleased to present you with your Fire Totem. Use this icon of power well in your travels, $N. \n\nJust remember, the power of the elemental plane serves those that respect it, and consumes those who do not. This is our way."},
[97288]={t="Unending Torment",o="Deliver the Abominable Head to Master Apothecary Faranell within the Undercity.",d="<As the creature falls, its head comes toppling off. It seems as if it has been reattached several times, and the connection gets weaker with each reconnection.\n\nSomeone in the Undercity would know more about this unique abomination.>",p="What have we here?",c="Oho! I believe I know this head. A cruel joke by our Dark Lady. A delicious one at that.\n\nI think I have a use for this."},
[97289]={t="Unending Torment",o="Bring the Head of the Baron to the body of Othmar in the Undercity.",d="We craft abomination heads all the time, but this one is special. It belonged to a Grand Marshal of the Alliance once. A particularly unpleasant one. Othmar, I believe its name was. The Dark Lady had the pleasure of dispatching this one herself.\n\nOoh the secrets it could tell if it could talk. And it can! If we reattach it to an appropriate host.\n\nGo ahead and place it next to the available body in the next room. But don't attach it. Not yet.",p="<The abomination remains lifeless without a head to control it.>",c="<The body twitches to life, panicking as it relives its final moments.>\n\nYou..."},
[97290]={t="Unending Torment",o="Report your findings to Master Apothecary Faranell in Undercity.",d="You... abomination...\n\nWhy should... help you...\n\nBe gone...",c="Not cooperating, eh? Excellent. I always love a challenge."},
[97291]={t="Unending Torment",o="Collect a Toxic Skullcap from Tawny Grisette in the Trade Quarter, Blisterweed near the Herbalism Trainer, and Essence of Agony from the poison vendor in the Rogues' Quarter for Master Apothecary Faranell in Undercity.",d="With the head reattached, all we need now is to bind it to the Dark Lady's will. This should not be a problem. The beast barely has brains left as it is after all the beatings it's taken.\n\nWe simply need to motivate it.\n\nFetch me a Toxic Skullcap from Miss Grisette in the Trade Quarter. Oh, and some Blisterweed from our local herbalist trainers, the Alliestars. Feel free to just take some, they owe me. And lastly a bit of Essence of Agony. Any old poison vendor should do.\n\nWe have a potion to make!",p="It will be ever so lovely to have our lost sheep returned to the fold, don't you think?",c="These will do nicely. We will see how much bravado our honored guest retains after he is subjected to my masterpiece."},
[97292]={t="Unending Torment",o="Inject the Hissing Serum into the system above Othmar's body for Master Apothecary Faranell.",d="I have concocted a lovely serum that our new guest is sure to find quite... stimulating.\n\nTake this. Feed it into the workings dripping from above him. Let's see if we can't show him why it's in his best interest to serve loyally.\n\nAnd try not to drop it. I can't afford a new assistant.",p="For Othmar's crimes against the Dark Lady, placing him under that oozing specimen is the least he deserves.\n\nAnd it's funny...",c="Excellent. We'll let his flesh simmer for awhile. Give him time to acclimate to his new home.\n\nI have no further use for the wretch for now, but we shall keep an eye on him. I have many plans for Othmar's future."},
[97326]={t="Rocks to Rests",o="Return 8 Smooth Boulders to Thra behind Grommash Hold.",d="Hey! You've got time to help us out! I know you do, I can tell by the way you smiled watching the game we're playing.\n\nThis spot behind Grommash Hold is nice because it's clear enough for us to set up our figures. But what stinks is we don't have enough rocks for chairs or tables.\n\nYou're big and strong... d'ya think you could carry back some medium-sized rocks, smooth enough to sit on if we need a rest?",p="It's nice to not have to always sit in the dirt!",c="How can you even hold all of those boulders!\n\nThose are great. Most even have a nice flat side, too. Now that you carried them all the way over here we can scoot them around in the dirt, right where we want 'em.\n\nThanks, $N!"},
[97485]={t="Traditions of the Bluff",o="Purchase a Bundle of Herbs from Nida the herbalist, a Bundle of Cedar Twigs from Nata the enchanting supplier, and Sinew Thread from Mahu the leatherworking supplier and Ceremonial Flint and Tinder from Naal the cooking supplier.\n\nCombine the items and sprinkle the incense off of Hunter's Rise.",d="Blessings of An'she, friend.\n\nWe tauren have a tradition of scattering incense to the winds and I was hoping you'd be interested in honoring this tradition.\n\nYou will need to craft the incense by purchasing herbs from Nida, cedar from Nata, sinew thread from Mahu in the mid rise, and ceremonial flint and tinder from Naal on the upper rise. Once you have these items, combine them and spread them off the south facing cliff of Hunter's Rise.\n\nYou will find a mat and incense at the ceremonial site.",p="There are many occasions one may choose to spread incense to the winds. You could be asking the Earthmother to watch over someone, bless a hunt, celebrate an occasion, or even to seek guidance from our ancestors.\n\nOr it could be something else entirely.\n\nThough the act is done with reverence, it is not strictly a ceremonial affair. Typically there are certain traditional steps observed when performing this act, but many tribes have differing practices.",c="You have done well.\n\nI thank you for taking the time to perform one of our time-honored traditions, skyborne. I hope that as you travel you will find plenty of occasions you wish to give thanks for.\n\nShould you ever wish to perform the ritual again, you should be able to repurchase the components I sent you to collect.\n\nGo with An'she's warmth."},
[97538]={t="Pigments for Paints",o="Tah Winterhoof in Thunder Bluff wants 30 Mirkweed Pods from Mirkfallon Lake.",d="Greetings, friend. I wonder if I may ask a favor of you? I have just run out of red pigment for my paints, and I am looking for one with younger hooves to make the long journey into the Stonetalon Mountains on my behalf.\n\nIn the middle of the mountain pass there lies a large circular lake, Mirkfallon Lake, that has a unique plant that grows within its waters. The pods of this plant, mirkweed, turn a vibrant red when dried. Gather the pods of this plant for me, and I will reward you well for your efforts."},
[97558]={t="Hides for the Forsaken",o="Bring Shelene Rhobart 8 Duskbat Wing Membranes, 6 Darkhound Hides and 3 Vile Fin Murloc Skin.",d="One part of undeath no one mentions is what happens when we are injured. How does the skin of an undead heal itself?\n\nWell, it doesn't.\n\nOurs is a cursed life, $N. We must take from the living to further our own existence.\n\nWhen we sustain an injury, we must replace our skin which usually means animal hides. Since different hide thicknesses are better for different places on our bodies a variety is key!\n\nBring me wing membranes of a duskbat, hides from a darkhound and skin of a Vile Fin murloc."},
[97963]={t="Camping 101: Alchemy",o="Speak with Nyassa Swiftdraught in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",d="So, you chose to cook up brews and potions as an Alchemist. I'm sure that'll come in handy in your travels.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste.",c="There you have it, you can now craft your very own Mana Well. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics."},
[97965]={t="Camping 101: First Aid",o="Speak with Naleeia Tattermend in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",d="So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a shaman.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives.",c="There you have it, you can now craft your very own First Aid Kit. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics."},
[97967]={t="Camping 101: Fishing",o="Speak with Fenn Fairweather in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",d="You might not think so, but your skill as a fisherman can actually come in handy at camp.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Fish Bowl for your camp. You can use this fixture to help provide a bit of joy to yourself and your fellow adventurers. A happy adventurer is a strong adventurer and I'm sure your combat capabilities will reflect that.",c="There you have it, you can now craft your very own Fish Bowl. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics."},
[97968]={t="Camping 101: Herbalism",o="Speak with Syriel Nightrain in Valanaar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.",d="Looks to me like you've gained some skill in herbalism. Picking flowers isn't just for dilly-dallying, you know. It can be useful... and profitable.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. High spirits are a key component to keeping healers and spellcasters in the fight, and an Incense Candle can provide a boost that magic users will surely appreciate.",c="There you have it, you can now craft your very own Incense Candle. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\n\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics."},
[98024]={t="Journey to the Crossroads",o="Report To Thork at The Crossroads in The Barrens.",d="After journeying here from the elemental plane, the problems our lands face may seem small. Rest assured, the dangers the horde faces are very real, and you will grow formidable should you survive your service.\n\nIf you'd like to get started doing some good in our world, travel southwest to the vast lands known as the Barrens. There is a settlement there known as the Crossroads. The proud citizens there are ever in need of aid.\n\nGo with honor, adventurer!",c="What's this? An elf? And you say the Warchief sent you?\n\n<Thork grunts sharply as he looks you up and down.>\n\nYou look a little skinny to me, but it matters not. Out here you'll either thrive and survive, or you'll die. That is the way of things in these lands."},
[98512]={t="Al'Aketh Assassins",o="Kill 10 Al'Aketh Assassins in the Shen'dar Highlands.",d="You there, stranger. Get low and keep quiet. We are not alone here.\n\nI was on patrol near the border and noticed that there are a number of Al'Aketh skulking around the house just up the hill there to the north. I don't know what they are doing here, but it can't be good.\n\nIf you want to make yourself useful, get in there and take them out. I'll wait here and watch your back.",c="I'm glad you made it back. That group of Al'Aketh looked like stone cold killers. \n\nThank you for your aid, I'll include your assistance in my report when I return to Valanaar."},
[99156]={t="Rear Guard Patrol",o="Bring Riptear's Heart to Deathguard Linnea.",d="Damn it all! A new report came in while you were on patrol. There has been a sighting of a rogue abomination wandering Eastern Tirisfal Glades, near Venomweb Vale.\n\nSomething is wrong. Abominations don't just slip through the Bulwark unnoticed.\n\nKeep this matter on a strictly need-to-know basis. That said, such a creature will not fall easily; you will need allies if you wish to be more than its next meal.\n\nSee this through, and you will be duly rewarded. Bring me its heart as proof of the deed.",p="Have you dealt with our little problem?",c="You are a testament to the cunning and coordination that all Forsaken possess--something the mindless Scourge will never have.\n\nPlease accept this as thanks for your efforts, as promised."},
[99196]={t="A Donation of Wool",p="The Windshapers are currently accepting donations for wool cloth.\n\nA donation of sixty pieces of wool cloth will net you full recognition by the Windshapers for your generosity. \n\nIf you have the sixty pieces of wool cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now."},
}
